WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能讲述的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.360
Oh, Angela.
噢，安吉拉。

9
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.860
Hi there.
你好呀。

10
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.080
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

11
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.660
Hello, hello.
你好，你好。

12
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.220
Is everybody ready for a garden party?
大家都准备好参加花园派对了吗？

13
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:36.960
Well, I am wearing my Connecticut casual outfit, so.
嗯，我穿的是康涅狄格州的休闲装，所以……

14
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.280
Good.
很好。

15
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:38.480
Good.
很好。

16
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:44.380
This is Season 8, Episode 4, written by Justin Spitzer and directed by Dave Rogers.
这是第八季第四集，由贾斯汀·斯皮策编剧，戴夫·罗杰斯执导。

17
00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.500
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

18
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.880
Andy throws a dignified garden party at Shroot Farms under the guise of impressing Robert California.
安迪在施鲁特农场举办了一场庄重的花园派对，借口是为了给罗伯特·加利福尼亚留下好印象。

19
00:00:52.480 --> 00:01:00.380
But it soon becomes clear that he is really trying to impress his parents, who clearly favor his younger brother, Walter Jr.
但很快大家就看出来，他其实是想给父母留下好印象，而他的父母显然更偏爱他的弟弟小沃尔特。

20
00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.680
Meanwhile, Pam and Angela discover they have chosen the same name for their unborn sons.
与此同时，帕姆和安吉拉发现她们为各自未出生的儿子取了同一个名字。

21
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.400
And Jim plays a very elaborate prank on Dwight.
吉姆还对德怀特搞了一个非常精心设计的恶作剧。

22
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.040
Very elaborate.
非常精心。

23
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.160
We'll get into it.
我们待会儿会细说。

24
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.080
But I was like, seriously, Jim?
当时我就想，吉姆，你是认真的吗？

25
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.180
I have so many things to say about it and so much mail to read.
我有很多话要说，还有很多邮件要读。

26
00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.940
I was going to say, I hope there was a fan mail flurry.
我正想说，希望粉丝来信像雪片一样飞来。

27
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:22.880
There certainly was.
确实如此。

28
00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:33.160
Well, listen, to kick things off for this episode, we have an interview with the one, the only, Walter Jr., Josh Groban.
听着，在这一集开始之前，我们采访了那位独一无二的小沃尔特——乔什·格罗班。

29
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.760
What a wonderful person.
真是个了不起的人。

30
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.920
We had the best time talking to him.
我们和他聊得非常开心。

31
00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.620
We can't wait for you to hear this interview.
迫不及待想让你们听到这段采访。

32
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.740
I was on a high all day after we did our interview.
采访结束后，我整天都处于兴奋状态。

33
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.220
Smiling all day.
笑了一整天。

34
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.520
Now, listen, Josh Groban, Grammy-nominated singer-songwriter.
听着，乔什·格罗班，格莱美提名的创作型歌手。

35
00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:57.460
In 2003, he won two Billboard Music Awards for Classical Crossover Artist of the Year and Classical Crossover Album of the Year for Closer.
2003年，他凭借《Closer》获得了两项公告牌音乐奖：年度古典跨界艺人和年度古典跨界专辑。

36
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:01.900
His first four solo albums all went multi-platinum.
他的前四张个人专辑全部获得了多白金销量认证。

37
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.940
And in 2007, he was the number one best-selling artist in the United States.
2007年，他是美国销量第一的艺人。

38
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:13.560
And as of 2022, he has sold over 25 million records worldwide.
截至2022年，他在全球的唱片销量已超过2500万张。

39
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:14.900
Wow.
哇。

40
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.980
I mean, seriously.
我是说，真的太厉害了。

41
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.380
In 2007, he starred in Natasha Pierre and the Great Comet of 1812 on Broadway.
2007年，他主演了百老汇音乐剧《娜塔莎、皮埃尔和1812年的大彗星》。

42
00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:27.420
He was nominated for a Tony Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role in a Musical.
他获得了托尼奖音乐剧最佳男主角提名。

43
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.540
And he is now currently starring in Sweeney Todd on Broadway.
他目前正在百老汇主演《理发师陶德》。

44
00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:37.880
It has been nominated for eight Tony Awards, including Best Actor in a Musical for Josh Groban.
该剧获得了八项托尼奖提名，其中包括乔什·格罗班的最佳音乐剧男主角提名。

45
00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.140
It is running right now through January 2024.
演出将持续到2024年1月。

46
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:44.500
I am going to get to see this in just a few weeks.
几周后我就能去看了。

47
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.900
I cannot wait.
我等不及了。

48
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.060
I know.
我知道。

49
00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.600
I wish I was with you.
真希望我也能和你一起去。

50
00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:49.340
I'm so bummed.
我太难过了。

51
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.660
You're going to have to tell us all about it.
你得把这一切都告诉我们。

52
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.420
I absolutely will.
我绝对会说的。

53
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:57.760
Well, I guess without further ado, here is our interview with Josh Groban.
好吧，我想事不宜迟，下面就是我们对乔什·格罗班的采访。

54
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.550
Oh, my gosh, Josh.
天哪，乔什。

55
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.230
Hello, Josh.
你好，乔什。

56
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.530
This is so exciting.
这太让人兴奋了。

57
00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.310
Angela and Jenna, I'm so excited to be with you.
安吉拉和珍娜，能和你们在一起我太激动了。

58
00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.710
It's been a really long time since I've seen either of you.
我已经很久没见到你们俩了。

59
00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:15.070
Angela and I did a kind of a web thing, a really fun comedy thing.
安吉拉和我做过一个网络短片，一个非常有趣的喜剧短片。

60
00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:15.670
A web series.
一个网络系列剧。

61
00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:20.150
Not too long after we filmed our episode, but it's been a really, really long time.
就在我们拍完那一集后不久，但那已经是真的很久很久以前的事了。

62
00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:26.010
And Jenna, thank you so much for reaching out and for asking me to be part of this.
还有珍娜，非常感谢你主动联系我，邀请我参与这个节目。

63
00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:26.470
Yes.
是的。

64
00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:29.470
I slid into your DMs on Instagram.
我在Instagram上私信了你。

65
00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:29.950
You did.
你确实这么做了。

66
00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:33.230
And I was so happy you got back to me.
你回复我的时候我太开心了。

67
00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.830
And I mean, I blew up Angela's phone.
我是说，我当时狂轰滥炸了安吉拉的手机。

68
00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.090
I was like, he wrote back.
我当时说，他回信了。

69
00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:37.430
She did.
她确实这么说了。

70
00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:37.970
He wrote back.
他回信了。

71
00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:38.710
He said yes.
他说愿意。

72
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.530
He said yes.
他说愿意。

73
00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.570
I saw it.
我看到了。

74
00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.370
I'm so thrilled.
我太激动了。

75
00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:45.030
And that was very similar to how I wound up being on The Office in general.
这和我当初参与《办公室》的过程非常相似。

76
00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:46.170
It was a DM slide.
也是通过私信联系上的。

77
00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.430
OK, we wanted to ask you about this.
好的，我们想问问你这件事。

78
00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:49.970
You have to share with everyone.
你得和大家分享一下。

79
00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:53.210
We always ask everyone, how did you get your part on The Office?
我们总是问每个人，你是怎么得到《办公室》里的角色的？

80
00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.550
So you have to tell the story.
所以你得讲讲这个故事。

81
00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.030
Well, I mean, I can imagine that I was very similar to
嗯，我想我和许多受邀参演该剧的人应该很像，

82
00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.170
many people who were asked to be on the show and that we were all just enormous fans of the show.
我们都是这部剧的超级粉丝。

83
00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:11.030
And so to get a request to say, hey, this might be a fun thing for you to do was just like finding the golden ticket.
所以当收到邀请说，嘿，这可能是一件很有趣的事情时，就像是找到了金奖券一样。

84
00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:11.990
It was an amazing thing.
那真是一件了不起的事情。

85
00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:15.890
So Mindy Kaling did the DM slide on the old Twitter.
所以明迪·卡灵在老版推特上给我发了私信。

86
00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:16.390
Remember Twitter?
还记得推特吗？

87
00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:16.870
Yep.
记得。

88
00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:17.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，记得。

89
00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.290
Those were the days.
那真是令人怀念的日子。

90
00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:28.230
And so Mindy sent me a message saying, hey, we're writing an episode and we think there might be a role that would be really fun for you.
明迪给我发消息说，嘿，我们正在写一集剧本，觉得有个角色可能很适合你，会很有趣。

91
00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.170
Are you in the L.A.
你这段时间在洛杉矶

92
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.190
area during this date?
附近吗？

93
00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.850
And I was on tour at that time.
当时我正在巡演。

94
00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.710
I was actually doing a really, really big tour at that time.
那时我实际上正在进行一场规模非常非常大的巡演。

95
00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:42.430
And so I really didn't think when she mentioned it that I would have any time at all.
所以当她提到这件事时，我真的以为我完全没时间。

96
00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.950
And it was going to absolutely crush my soul to not be able to do it.
如果不能参加的话，我一定会心碎不已的。

97
00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.890
But it landed right when I was playing L.A.
但拍摄时间正好赶上我在洛杉矶演出。

98
00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:58.450
And so during my time off between shows, I was able to take a little road trip up to Shroot FarMs.
所以在我演出间隙的休息时间里，我得以去了一趟施鲁特农场。

99
00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:04.490
And it was the best recharge I could have possibly imagined.
那是我能想象到的最好的充电方式。

100
00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:05.250
It was so fun.
真的太有趣了。

101
00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.390
It was I mean, I talk about it even to this day.
我的意思是，直到今天我还会提起这件事。

102
00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:13.170
It was really one of the one of my most favorite days, you know, that I've ever had in the business or out of the business.
那真的是我人生中最棒的日子之一，无论是在演艺圈内外，你懂的。

103
00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:13.990
It was just the beSt.
那简直太棒了。

104
00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:14.790
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

105
00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:16.110
So what made it so fun?
那是什么让你觉得那么开心呢？

106
00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.990
What what do you love about it?
你最喜欢它的哪一点？

107
00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:26.650
Well, I mean, having done now some TV since then, I can tell you that shooting like at a lovely outdoor estate is a delight.
嗯，我是说，在那之后我也拍过一些电视节目，我可以告诉你，在美丽的户外庄园拍摄真是一种享受。

108
00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:34.090
Like to not be to not be at a soundstage, to not have to spend 15 hours in a little, you know,
不用待在摄影棚里，不用在那个小小的、你知道的、

109
00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:43.390
box of a room where you're not seeing daylight and to be able to shoot a on a beautiful kind of setting.
像盒子一样的房间里待上15个小时，见不到一点阳光，而是能在那种优美的环境下拍摄。

110
00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:52.070
But then also, again, as a fan of the show to sometimes when you make a guest appearance on a show, you're doing it with one person or two,
但另一方面，作为该剧的粉丝，有时候你去客串一部剧，你可能只和其中一两个人搭戏，

111
00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:57.350
two people from the show and you're part of like a little arc that doesn't involve other people in the caSt.
剧组里的两个人，你只是参与了一个不涉及其他演员的小情节。

112
00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:13.210
And so to be part of a everybody together doing a party scene meant that as a fanboy of the show, I got to sit and just be around like the entire cast for the entirety of the day.
所以能参与到大家聚在一起拍摄的派对场景，意味着作为一个剧迷，我能坐在那里，整整一天都和整个剧组待在一起。

113
00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:20.930
And so it was just, you know, I felt like I'd I felt like I'd kind of like won an auction or something that like, you know,
所以那种感觉，你知道，我觉得我好像赢得了什么拍卖会一样，你知道，

114
00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:23.350
come come hang at Shrewd Farms with the cast of The Office.
就是那种“来施鲁特农场和《办公室》剧组一起玩”的机会。

115
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:25.490
It was the beSt.
那真是太棒了。

116
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.490
And of course, because you're sitting around a lot during shooting of something,
当然，因为拍摄过程中你会有很多时间坐在那儿，

117
00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:36.370
there's just a lot of time to just get to know everybody and get to know the writers and and the wonderful crew and and just chat with everybody.
所以有很多时间去了解每个人，去认识编剧们、很棒的剧组工作人员，和大家聊天。

118
00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.870
And it was just such a dream.
那简直就像一场梦。

119
00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:42.050
I loved location episodes just for that reason, too.
我也因为这个原因特别喜欢外景拍摄的剧集。

120
00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.690
There was a lot of hanging out.
我们有很多时间聚在一起。

121
00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:47.550
I have a picture of us just all casually on the porch at Shrewd FarMs.
我有一张照片，是我们大家都很随意地坐在施鲁特农场的门廊上。

122
00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:47.830
Yeah.
是啊。

123
00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:48.830
And we're just chatting.
我们当时就在聊天。

124
00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.850
And we were all so charmed by you, Josh.
而且我们都被你迷住了，乔什。

125
00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.010
We were so excited.
我们当时太兴奋了。

126
00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.410
And I know I was trying to play it cool.
我知道我当时在努力装作若无其事。

127
00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.850
I'm sure Jenna, too, because we're two of the biggest dorks ever.
我相信珍娜也是，因为我们俩是史上最大的书呆子。

128
00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:01.850
But you were instantly you were instantly Andy's brother.
但你瞬间就成为了安迪的兄弟。

129
00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.090
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

130
00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:04.290
It was so perfect.
太完美了。

131
00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:09.970
I loved that they wrote, you know, sometimes I play like myself.
我喜欢他们写的剧本，你知道，有时候我演的是我自己。

132
00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:10.410
Yeah.
是啊。

133
00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:11.330
Like Parks and Rec.
就像在《公园与游憩》里那样。

134
00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:12.290
You played yourself.
你演了你自己。

135
00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:13.850
Like in Parks and Rec.
就像在《公园与游憩》里。

136
00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:13.990
Yeah.
是啊。

137
00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.010
I played myself.
我演了我自己。

138
00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:16.570
And Glee, I played myself.
还有《欢乐合唱团》，我也演了我自己。

139
00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:23.930
And I'm just one of those people like because my music side is like so serious, like whenever somebody wants me to play a bizarro version of me,
我就是那种人，因为我的音乐那一面非常严肃，所以每当有人想让我演一个古怪版本的我时，

140
00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:27.610
it just like lets me kind of let that other side play around a little bit.
这反而让我能释放出另一面去玩玩。

141
00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.450
And so I say yes to playing myself weirdly sometimes.
所以我有时候会奇怪地答应去演我自己。

142
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:38.870
This was an opportunity like this was really, really fun to, you know, to play Andy's brother.
这是一个机会，演安迪的兄弟真的、真的非常有趣。

143
00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:49.130
And when Mindy, Mindy and BJ kind of laid out for me, you know, what the story is, the jealousy, the sibling rivalry and the jealousy and and why, you know, I got to be Walter Jr.
当敏迪、敏迪和BJ跟我讲故事梗概时，你知道，关于嫉妒、兄弟间的竞争，以及为什么，你知道，我成了小沃尔特。

144
00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.950
And they passed over, you know, Ed.
而他们跳过了，你知道，艾德。

145
00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:52.950
Yeah, the namesake.
对，那个同名的人。

146
00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:53.590
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

147
00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:57.990
It just every bit of it was so funny to me.
这一切对我来说都太搞笑了。

148
00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:01.170
My brother and I have the same birthday four years apart.
我和我哥哥是同一天生日，差了四岁。

149
00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:10.550
So we have had we've we had our own like little sibling, like we've never had any rivalry, but he's now like my best friend and he's like the beSt.
所以我们有自己那种小小的兄弟情，虽然我们从来没有过竞争，他现在是我最好的朋友，他简直棒极了。

150
00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:18.450
But like when you get like when you have to share a birthday, you know, there's that there's that weird sibling tension when it's like four and eight, you know, and.
但当你不得不共用一个生日时，你知道，当你是四岁和八岁的时候，那种奇怪的兄弟间的紧张感就出现了，你知道。

151
00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:19.530
Yeah.
是啊。

152
00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:22.950
How do you do that party for both a four year old and an eight year old?
你是怎么给四岁和八岁的孩子同时办派对的？

153
00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.050
Yeah.
是啊。

154
00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:33.530
We discovered very early on that all, you know, because parties are organized by the parents at that age, the kids were not we're not in charge of presents that we're just kids.
我们很早就发现，因为那个年纪的派对都是家长组织的，孩子们并不负责礼物，他们只是孩子。

155
00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:43.730
So we realized very early on that the parents, if they knew that it was also big brother Josh's birthday, they would bring a little extra present.
所以我们很早就意识到，如果家长们知道那天也是大哥哥乔什的生日，他们会多带一份小礼物。

156
00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:50.790
You know, we got we got to bring an extra present because it's also so we had we we figured out early on that same birthday meant double the presents.
你知道，我们得带一份额外的礼物，因为那天也是……所以我们很早就发现，同一天生日意味着双倍的礼物。

157
00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:55.110
And so so we we mean we had a little deal.
所以我们……我们达成了一个小协议。

158
00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:56.250
We made it work.
我们成功做到了。

159
00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.030
You made it work.
你们成功做到了。

160
00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.050
Yes, we made it work.
是的，我们做到了。

161
00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:05.150
One of the things I loved in rewatching this episode was that Andy's brother seems like he genuinely just loves Andy.
重温这一集时，我最喜欢的一点是安迪的弟弟看起来是真的非常爱安迪。

162
00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.890
He's his Bronard and he was so excited to meet Tuna.
他是他的好兄弟，而且他见到“金枪鱼”时特别兴奋。

163
00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.010
Yes, exactly.
没错，确实如此。

164
00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.110
He clearly looks up to his brother.
他显然很崇拜他的哥哥。

165
00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.670
And I thought that was really nice.
我觉得这一点真的很棒。

166
00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:21.070
It's like whatever Andy's feeling, I don't I didn't feel like his brother was trying to stir the pot, you know, totally.
感觉无论安迪有什么情绪，我都不觉得他弟弟是在故意挑拨离间，完全没有。

167
00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:25.370
I think that a lot of it is, you know, is is within Andy.
我觉得很大程度上，你知道，这都是安迪自己的问题。

168
00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:29.790
There's there's a lot of there's a lot of stuff that Andy's kind of like, you know, needs therapy about.
安迪身上有很多……有很多东西是需要接受心理治疗的。

169
00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:32.390
But it's it's and that's that can happen.
但这……这确实会发生。

170
00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.910
And maybe at some point there was a little bit of that rub.
也许在某个时刻，他们之间确实有过一点摩擦。

171
00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.550
But I think that now it's like everybody's grown up.
但我认为现在大家都长大了。

172
00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.750
And I think that truly I felt one of the things I loved about Walter Jr.
而且我真心觉得，关于小沃尔特，我最喜欢的一点是……

173
00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:46.530
Is that like he's like this super talented golden retriever that just like doesn't know.
他就像一只超级有天赋的金毛寻回犬，只是他自己不知道。

174
00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:49.030
He's like, oh, yeah, sure.
他就像是，哦，好的，没问题。

175
00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:53.930
I'll go fetch that acoustic guitar and, you know, sing this sing this beautiful angelic song for all of you.
我去把那把木吉他拿来，然后为你们所有人唱这首……这首美妙的天使般的歌。

176
00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:58.330
And Andy is just eating him up inside, you know, and yeah,
而安迪在内心深处对他嫉妒得要命，你知道，是的。

177
00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:05.730
I think that that kind of lack of awareness was one of the things that really made that dynamic really adorable and really fun.
我认为那种缺乏自觉的状态，正是让那种互动变得非常可爱和有趣的原因之一。

178
00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:10.730
And, you know, I think I think the parents knew better a little bit, but I don't think Walter Jr.
而且，你知道，我觉得父母多少是知道一点的，但我不觉得小沃尔特

179
00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:11.190
knew better.
知道。

180
00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:11.910
I think Walter Jr.
我觉得小沃尔特

181
00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.350
is just just, you know, living his dream.
只是……你知道，活在他自己的梦想里。

182
00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:20.270
And it's like there's always those people out there that just have that little extra serotonin that you're just like, how that must be nice.
就像总有那么一些人，他们天生就比别人多那么一点血清素，让你觉得，哇，那一定很不错。

183
00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:27.710
How do you, how do you, God, if I could live in that brain for just one day, you know, that would be really, really fun.
你怎么……你怎么……天哪，如果我能在那样的脑子里住上一天，你知道，那一定会非常、非常有意思。

184
00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.710
And I think that, you know, Walter Jr.
而且我觉得，你知道，小沃尔特

185
00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.510
is one of those people where it's just like he keeps falling up.
就是那种总是能顺风顺水的人。

186
00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:32.930
Yeah.
是啊。

187
00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:36.550
And Andy's just had to be kind of next to that, you know, at all times.
而安迪不得不一直待在他身边，你知道，随时随地。

188
00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:41.670
And a side note to that, which is really funny because now I'm doing Sweeney Todd is that, you know,
顺便提一下，这真的很有趣，因为我现在正在演《理发师陶德》，你知道，

189
00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:45.030
one of my other very favorite episodes of The Office is the Sweeney Todd episode.
我最喜欢的《办公室》剧集之一就是《理发师陶德》那一集。

190
00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:52.850
And it's one that we all kind of quote and and love very much backstage at our Sweeney Todd is that, of course, Andy, you know, is in Sweeney Todd.
那是我们在《理发师陶德》后台经常引用并且非常喜欢的一集，当然，安迪在《理发师陶德》里演的是……

191
00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:53.290
Yes.
是的。

192
00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:54.810
And is Antony in Sweeney Todd.
安东尼在《理发师陶德》里。

193
00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.310
And now you're in Sweeney Todd, but you're the lead.
现在你也在演《理发师陶德》，但你是主角。

194
00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.810
And you're on Broadway.
而且你是在百老汇演出。

195
00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:00.270
Yes.
是的。

196
00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.370
So you have bested him again.
所以你又一次胜过他了。

197
00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.050
I have bested him yet again.
我又一次胜过他了。

198
00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:09.150
And that is the universe being so weird and so wonderful.
这就是宇宙的神奇与美妙之处。

199
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:12.050
And so, yes, yeah, it's it's great.
所以，是的，这太棒了。

200
00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:17.170
But and I'm I'm hoping at some point Ed and I can really kind of sit down and have a proper talk and hug it out.
但我希望在某个时候，我和艾德能真正坐下来，好好谈谈，然后拥抱和解。

201
00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:19.950
That would be awesome.
那太棒了。

202
00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:23.210
When you were on set, Josh, did you ever break in a scene?
乔什，你在片场的时候，演戏时笑场过吗？

203
00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:24.170
Oh, yeah.
哦，有啊。

204
00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:24.870
All the time.
经常。

205
00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:26.250
Oh, yeah, absolutely.
哦，有，绝对有。

206
00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:32.590
I guess one of my questions for you, because I was only I did two episodes and spent a day doing each episode.
我有个问题想问你们，因为我当时只拍了两集，每集花了一天时间。

207
00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:38.910
But I kind of wanted to ask you guys as well, you know, was that was there always room for improv on your days?
但我其实也想问问你们，你们在片场的时候，是不是总有即兴发挥的空间？

208
00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.450
Because because the scripts were brilliant.
因为剧本写得太精彩了。

209
00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:47.250
Each one, every time I read it, it was so conversational and it felt so natural.
每一集，我每次读的时候，都觉得对话感很强，非常自然。

210
00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:54.290
And there were oftentimes things that were written that if I hadn't known it was written, I would think, oh, that must have been an improvised line.
而且经常会有一些台词，如果我不知道那是写好的，我肯定会觉得，哦，那一定是即兴发挥的。

211
00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.770
And that's just that's just how wonderful it was.
剧本就是写得这么好。

212
00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:00.730
But there was such wonderful improv happening at Shroot FarMs.
但在施鲁特农场拍摄时，确实有很多精彩的即兴发挥。

213
00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:06.230
Everybody was just kind of pitching things and and even off camera, just so everybody's just so funny.
每个人都在出谋划策，即使在镜头外，大家也都特别幽默。

214
00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:18.170
Kate Flannery was always finding new ways to like get me, you know, and with like the idea of like pulling my vocal cords out of my throat, you know, that kind of thing.
凯特·弗兰纳里总是能想出新花样来整我，你知道的，比如想把我的声带从喉咙里扯出来之类的，就是那种感觉。

215
00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:28.230
And so, yeah, I mean, was that always encouraged or was that something that kind of developed over time or or was that just the writing made it seem that way at all times?
所以，我想问，这种即兴发挥是一直被鼓励的，还是随着时间推移慢慢形成的，又或者只是因为剧本写得让人感觉像即兴的？

216
00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:29.950
It was sort of all of those things.
这几种情况都有。

217
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:35.670
I mean, it did always start with an amazing script, but it was always a living, breathing thing.
我的意思是，虽然总是以精彩的剧本为基础，但它始终是一个鲜活的、不断演变的东西。

218
00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:43.690
So the writers of that episode and the producers would come down and they were always pitching alternate lines.
所以那一集的编剧和制片人会到现场，他们总是会提出备选台词。

219
00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:44.090
Pitching.
提供建议。

220
00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:44.690
Yeah.
没错。

221
00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:49.750
And they would throw them out to the actors or the actors might have an idea in the moment.
他们会把这些建议抛给演员，或者演员在拍摄时也会有自己的想法。

222
00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.190
And it was always allowed.
而且这总是被允许的。

223
00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:51.810
Yeah.
对。

224
00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:55.850
You know, as long as we had gotten it in a scripted way, at least once.
只要我们至少按剧本演过一遍就行。

225
00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:56.430
Yeah.
没错。

226
00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:57.670
Then we could play around.
之后我们就可以自由发挥了。

227
00:12:58.150 --> 00:12:58.510
Right.
对。

228
00:12:58.870 --> 00:12:59.790
That's really cool.
那真的很酷。

229
00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:05.630
And also just being kind of like an outsider in the group, I had not done a lot of acting at that time.
而且作为团队里的一个外来者，我当时并没有多少表演经验。

230
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.730
And I'd certainly not done a lot of comedy acting at that time.
而且我当时肯定没怎么演过喜剧。

231
00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:15.270
And so to be around so many very funny, very talented people, we got to like share stories about like our different worlds.
所以能和这么多非常有趣、非常有才华的人在一起，我们有机会分享彼此不同世界的故事。

232
00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.650
Like, so what's touring like, you know?
比如，巡演是什么样的？

233
00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:24.770
And so, you know, it actually kind of turned into like a real garden party, but like we just, we were, you know, just getting yogurt from craft.
所以，这真的变成了一场真正的花园派对，虽然我们只是在休息区拿酸奶吃。

234
00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.970
And, you know, it was just, it was just like really, really fun.
而且，真的，真的非常非常有趣。

235
00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:27.850
Really cool.
真的很酷。

236
00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:28.730
It was a hot day though.
不过那天天气很热。

237
00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:29.170
I remember that.
我记得。

238
00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:30.910
It was so hot that day.
那天热得要命。

239
00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:38.650
I found an email that Jenna and I traded back and forth about how hot it was and how that they had these huge tubes of air.
我翻到了一封我和珍娜当时互发的邮件，里面提到了天气有多热，还有他们准备了那些巨大的送风管。

240
00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.050
Yeah.
是啊。

241
00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.510
And we were all fighting about where you could sit.
我们都在争抢座位。

242
00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.290
So the tube of air would hit you.
为了能吹到那个送风管的风。

243
00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:51.290
And they turned them on whenever we took a break in scenes and everyone would like go around the tube, except in this email, I said, unfortunately,
每当我们休息时，他们就会打开风管，大家都围着风管转，除了在邮件里我提到的，不幸的是，

244
00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.970
Ellie was sitting basically right on top of the tube.
艾莉当时基本上就坐在风管口上。

245
00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:58.410
Like the tube kind of came right out to her chair and she was freezing.
那个风管口正好对着她的椅子，她都快冻僵了。

246
00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.730
And the rest of us were like, pull the tube this way.
而我们其他人都在喊，把风管往这边挪挪。

247
00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:01.610
We're burning up.
我们要热死了。

248
00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.770
Apparently the tubes were a big deal during the shoot.
看来那些送风管在拍摄期间确实很重要。

249
00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:08.230
Wow.
哇。

250
00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.070
And she, she was even peppier in those scenes.
而且她在那些戏份里表现得甚至更有活力。

251
00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.870
And that's the reason, that's the reason why.
这就是原因，这就是原因所在。

252
00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.090
Oh my God.
天哪。

253
00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:15.950
That's, that's so funny.
那真是，那真是太搞笑了。

254
00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:18.470
Everybody gathering around the, the coolant tube.
大家都围在那个冷却管旁边。

255
00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:20.350
Yeah, it was, it was very, very hot.
是啊，当时真的，真的非常非常热。

256
00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:25.870
You said you hadn't done a lot of acting, but you had just been in crazy, stupid love with Steve Carell.
你说过你没怎么演过戏，但你刚和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔一起演了《疯狂愚蠢的爱》。

257
00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:27.270
That's actually true.
那倒是真的。

258
00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.090
Which is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

259
00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:32.330
Which was like one of my first things that I ever did, you know, outside of music.
那算是我在音乐之外做的第一件事吧，你知道的。

260
00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:36.690
And that was not a DM slide getting, Steve, Steve did not, did not.
而且那可不是私信勾搭来的，史蒂夫，史蒂夫他没有，真的没有。

261
00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:37.410
It was proper.
那是正儿八经的试镜。

262
00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:40.250
Did not slide into my DMs for that role.
他没有为了那个角色给我发私信。

263
00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.810
I so wish that was the story behind that though.
我真希望背后的故事是那样的。

264
00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.750
Can we just say that that's what it was?
我们能就这么说吗？

265
00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.110
I want to rewrite history.
我想改写历史。

266
00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.050
No, here's the, here's the thing.
不，事情是这样的。

267
00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:52.550
No, it was, that was such a fun shoot as well.
不，那次拍摄真的非常有趣。

268
00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.070
It was again, just a, just a couple of days.
而且又一次，只是，只是几天的时间。

269
00:14:54.230 --> 00:14:58.590
We shot at the Glendale Galleria and we shot all night at like an El Torito.
我们在格伦代尔广场购物中心拍摄，还在一家 El Torito 餐厅拍了一整晚。

270
00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.610
I know the Glendale Galleria.
我知道格伦代尔广场购物中心。

271
00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:01.290
Yeah.
是啊。

272
00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:01.930
Yeah.
是啊。

273
00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:02.830
The Glendale Galleria.
格伦代尔广场购物中心。

274
00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:08.610
Every time I drive by it, getting onto the 101, I was like, yeah, that's, I had a lot of tortilla chips.
每次我开车经过那里，准备上 101 号公路时，我都会想，没错，我当时吃了很多玉米片。

275
00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:09.510
Yeah.
是啊。

276
00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.670
That's where I had my first on-screen kiss.
那是我第一次银幕初吻的地方。

277
00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.210
But weren't you a theater major?
但你不是戏剧专业的吗？

278
00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:20.750
I was a theater major, but I got plucked out of college when I, when I got a recording contract.
我是戏剧专业的，但我拿到唱片合约时就被学校“挖”走了。

279
00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:27.590
It was a weird fork in the road and one that has, you know, afforded me some extraordinary experiences like this one.
那是人生中一个奇怪的分岔路口，但也正是它，你知道的，让我获得了像这次一样非凡的经历。

280
00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:31.290
But it was my first love was, was doing theater.
但我最初的爱，一直是戏剧表演。

281
00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.430
My first, my, and my first love before that was doing comedy and doing improv.
我最初的，我在此之前的初恋是喜剧和即兴表演。

282
00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:38.010
I was very lucky to do a lot of improv in high school and junior high school.
我很幸运，在高中和初中时做了很多即兴表演。

283
00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:44.010
It kind of like got me out of my shell when I was really, really shy and having a hard time making friends and my grades weren't great.
它让我从那种非常非常害羞、难以交朋友、成绩也不太好的状态中走了出来。

284
00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.530
And I just was like kind of trapped.
当时我感觉自己被困住了。

285
00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:53.450
And joining like the school improv troupe and being able to be part of like a youth second city class when I was like, you know, 11.
加入学校的即兴表演剧团，并在我 11 岁时参加了青年第二城剧团的课程。

286
00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:58.630
And, and being part of the LA Connection Comedy Theater in the Valley when I was, you know, 13 and 14.
还有在我 13、14 岁时，参加了山谷地区的 LA Connection 喜剧剧场。

287
00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:06.790
Like those kinds of improv games were so good for that muscle in my brain that had not been activated at that point.
那些即兴游戏对我大脑中当时尚未被激活的区域非常有帮助。

288
00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:13.430
And was so great for me being social and being able to, because improv is all about kind of saying yes and really listening and being part of that.
这对我的社交能力大有裨益，因为即兴表演的核心就是“说是”，学会倾听并融入其中。

289
00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:17.770
And when you're closed off as a kid, those things kind of get stunted.
当你还是个孩子却封闭自己时，这些能力往往会发育迟缓。

290
00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:25.770
And so it was finding the rhythm of comedy was something that really got me out of my shell long before finding the rhythm of, of music.
所以，在找到音乐的节奏感之前，是喜剧的节奏感让我真正走出了自我。

291
00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:33.550
And, and then that fork in the road happened and it's been the most incredible journey of my life to be able to be a solo artist and make music and sing for people.
后来，那个分岔路口出现了，能成为一名独唱艺人，创作音乐并为人们歌唱，这是我一生中最不可思议的旅程。

292
00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:42.170
But every time I've had an opportunity to step back into, you know, the camaraderie of, of acting and comedy and theater, it's an absolute blaSt.
但每当有机会重回表演、喜剧和戏剧那种并肩作战的氛围中时，我总是乐在其中。

293
00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.510
You were speaking to my improv heart.
你真是说到我的即兴表演心坎里去了。

294
00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.490
My improv heart is singing.
我的即兴表演之心在歌唱。

295
00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:55.830
Um, I moved around a lot as a kid and one of the ways I would connect is through improv class or sketch comedy and just being an outsider.
嗯，我小时候经常搬家，而我融入环境的方式之一就是通过即兴表演课或小品喜剧，因为我总是个局外人。

296
00:16:55.990 --> 00:17:03.170
It was a way in, um, and I actually had my kids do an improv class and it was so adorable.
这是一种切入点，嗯，我实际上让我孩子们也去上了即兴表演课，太可爱了。

297
00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:09.490
And at the same time, the very first minute I sat there on their performance night and they came out and they started doing these improv games that I had done.
与此同时，在他们表演的那晚，我坐在那里的第一分钟，当他们走出来开始做那些我曾经做过的即兴游戏时。

298
00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.690
I started crying.
我开始哭了。

299
00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.110
My husband was like, I don't think you should be crying.
我丈夫说，我觉得你不该哭的。

300
00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:17.810
Like, but I was just like, I'm so moved that these same games are there and it's yes.
但我就是觉得，看到这些相同的游戏还在传承，而且那种“说是”的精神还在，我真的太感动了。

301
00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:24.930
And, and being in the moment and listening and, and trust, you know, it's, it, there's so much trust involved in it.
还有，活在当下，学会倾听，还有信任，你知道，这其中涉及太多的信任了。

302
00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.970
And the idea is nothing like it in the world.
这种理念在世界上是独一无二的。

303
00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:34.570
The idea of going out, not knowing what's going to happen and trusting yourself and trusting the people that are around you.
那种走上台，不知道会发生什么，却依然信任自己、信任身边伙伴的理念。

304
00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:40.050
I just recently did four or five performances of this wonderful show that was on Broadway.
我最近刚在那部百老汇精彩剧目中演了四五场。

305
00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:48.450
It's not there anymore called Freestyle Love Supreme, which is kind of a music, it was like a music improv show that Lin-Manuel Miranda and a number of other incredible, uh,
那部剧现在已经停演了，叫《自由式爱至上》（Freestyle Love Supreme），它算是一种音乐即兴表演，是由林-曼努尔·米兰达（Lin-Manuel Miranda）和一些其他了不起的……呃，

306
00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:50.910
freestyle rappers and musicians kind of put together.
自由式说唱歌手和音乐人共同创作的。

307
00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.250
And it's, it's comedy, it's rap, it's music.
它融合了喜剧、说唱和音乐。

308
00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:56.910
And they said, Hey, will you come out and like sing an improvised love song every night?
他们当时问我：嘿，你愿意每晚都上台即兴唱一首情歌吗？

309
00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:57.950
We'll interview an audience member.
我们会采访一位观众。

310
00:17:57.950 --> 00:17:59.270
And then we'll come up with a song together.
然后我们一起创作一首歌。

311
00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:06.310
And every single time, you know, I asked Lin, like, do you have any advice for how to make this successful?
每一次，你知道，我都会问林：你有什么建议能让表演成功吗？

312
00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.490
And he said, yeah, the first thing is take a half shot of whiskey.
他说：有，第一件事就是先喝半杯威士忌。

313
00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.970
Second thing is don't prepare anything.
第二件事就是什么都别准备。

314
00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:20.430
You're going to be really tempted to write lines that you're going to want to, you know, shoehorn into the song because you think they're clever and whatever else.
你会非常想写好台词，想把它们硬塞进歌里，因为你觉得那些台词很聪明，或者其他什么原因。

315
00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:28.470
And he said, that part of your brain that has lines prepared is going to be clashing with the part of your brain that's going to be receiving what the,
他说，你大脑中负责准备台词的那部分，会和你大脑中负责接收当晚现场反馈、接收观众反馈的那部分发生冲突。

316
00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:30.770
what the night is giving you and what the audience is giving you.
这会让你卡壳。

317
00:18:30.850 --> 00:18:32.010
And it's going to make you stumble.
所以，带着清醒的头脑、开放的心态和充分的信任上台，灵感自然会来。

318
00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:36.630
So go out there with a clear mind, open heart, and a lot of trust and it'll come.
结果第一次上台时，效果简直好得惊人。

319
00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.670
And then like the first time I went out there, it just, it was like gangbusters.
太棒了。

320
00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:41.030
It was great.
第二次，我心想那只是运气好。

321
00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:42.370
Second, I'm thinking that was a fluke.
但第二晚效果依然好得惊人。

322
00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:43.930
And the second night it was gangbusters.
就是这样，每次都是如此，你只需要相信灵感会眷顾你。

323
00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:49.170
And that's just, and it just, it was that way every time you just trust that it's going to be there for you.
而且这对于孩子们来说很有意义。

324
00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.070
And it's for kids.
这就是为什么我如此支持年轻人去体验这类活动，因为那些时刻，那些“啊哈”时刻，

325
00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:57.430
It's why I'm such a proponent of these kinds of experiences for young students, because those moments, those aha moments,
那些灵光一现的瞬间，能够改变一个年轻人的一生。

326
00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:02.350
those little light bulb flips change the course of a young person's life.
即使他们将来并不从事艺术、喜剧、戏剧或音乐行业。

327
00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:06.150
Even if they don't go into the arts and comedy and theater and music.
事实上，很多时候他们确实不会从事这些行业，但这会让他们成为更全面、更自信的医生或律师。

328
00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:12.970
In fact, many times they won't, but it will make them a far more, you know, well-rounded and confident doctor and lawyer.
那些在非创意领域工作的人也会来找我，说艺术、喜剧、即兴表演和音乐剧这些经历改变了他们的人生轨迹。

329
00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:21.670
And the people that come up to me in jobs that are not considered creative that said that arts and comedy and improv and musical theater and all that stuff changed the course of their life.
这真是太不可思议了。

330
00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:22.690
It's incredible.
乔什，我本来在采访开始时尽量不表现得太像个小迷妹。

331
00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:29.010
Josh, I was trying not to fangirl too hard at the beginning of this interview.
但现在你让我彻底破功了。

332
00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:30.550
And now you have made it impossible.
好吧。

333
00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:31.530
Yeah.
算了吧。

334
00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:32.330
Forget it.
算了吧。

335
00:19:32.590 --> 00:19:33.190
Forget it.
好吧，我无话可说了。

336
00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.190
Well, I am speechless.
那太美好了。

337
00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:35.970
That was beautiful.
我也在努力克制自己别那样做。

338
00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:37.710
I'm trying not to do the same thing.
我想说，还有一个非常……我想想，我提到了“洛杉矶连接喜剧剧场”（LA Connection Comedy Theater），那是个很棒的地方。

339
00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:43.830
I will say there's also a really, I think, so I mentioned the LA Connection Comedy Theater, which is a wonderful place.
我在那儿上了几个月的课，也参与了一些演出。

340
00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.830
I spent like a few months doing classes there and doing some stuff there.
那时我大概16岁。

341
00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:47.790
I was like 16.
他们对我非常好，给了我一个绝佳的机会。

342
00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:50.870
They were really cool to me and they really provided me with a wonderful opportunity there.
我记得剧场大楼侧面有一幅很奇怪的壁画，画的是我和其他在那儿待过的校友。

343
00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:58.650
I think there's a very odd mural of me on the side of the building, like me and some other alumni that went there.
我想威尔·法瑞尔（Will Ferrell）也在上面。

344
00:19:58.770 --> 00:20:01.430
I think Will Ferrell is painted up there.
马修·派瑞（Matthew Perry）也在上面。

345
00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.970
I think Matthew Perry is painted up there.
关于上面画的是我还是基努·里维斯（Keanu Reeves）还有些争议，但我并不觉得基努·里维斯去过“洛杉矶连接喜剧剧场”。

346
00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:12.830
There is some discussion of whether it's me or Keanu Reeves painted up there, but I don't think Keanu Reeves went to the LA Connection Comedy Theater.
我觉得这是个“妈妈侦探”时刻，珍娜。

347
00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:16.190
I think this is a mom detective moment, Jenna.
我觉得我们需要开车过去看看。

348
00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.350
I think we need to drive over there.
我们会帮你查清楚的。

349
00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:18.610
We will check this out for you.
我记得它就在文图拉大道（Ventura Boulevard）上。

350
00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:20.730
I believe it's on Ventura Boulevard.
我记得它就在文图拉大道（Ventura Boulevard）上。

351
00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:28.090
And it's like directly across from like one of those Halloween, you know, costume emporium stores, you know.
它就在那些万圣节服装专卖店的对面，你知道的。

352
00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:38.290
Somebody sent it to me on Twitter and then I was looking for a costume last minute, last Halloween, and I was like, oh yeah, my girlfriend just sent me this picture.
有人在推特上发给我，去年万圣节我临时要找套服装，我就想，哦对了，我女朋友刚发过我这张照片。

353
00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:41.110
Your listeners can't look at it, but this is the wall.
听众们看不到，但这面墙就是这样。

354
00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:41.670
Yeah.
没错。

355
00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:42.330
Yeah.
是啊。

356
00:20:42.530 --> 00:20:47.230
If you send that to us, we'll put it on the Office Ladies pod Instagram.
如果你发给我们，我们会把它放到《办公室女士》播客的 Instagram 上。

357
00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:48.150
Yes.
好的。

358
00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.130
That's you.
那就是你。

359
00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.390
That is you.
那确实是你。

360
00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:52.490
But it could be Keanu as well.
但也可能是基努。

361
00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.810
But it could be Keanu.
但也可能是基努。

362
00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:55.210
It could be Keanu.
可能是基努。

363
00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:56.170
It could be a combo.
也可能是两者的结合。

364
00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:59.810
What we need to find out is if Keanu ever took improv class there.
我们需要查清楚的是基努有没有在那里上过即兴表演课。

365
00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:02.590
If he didn't, then it's definitely you.
如果他没上过，那肯定就是你了。

366
00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:04.190
And Matthew Perry, my goodness.
还有马修·派瑞，天哪。

367
00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:07.610
I have to say Matthew Perry also kind of looks like Keanu.
我得说马修·派瑞看起来也有点像基努。

368
00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.770
But also kind of looks like Dwight.
但也有一点像德怀特。

369
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:13.290
Because his hair, the way his hair is parted.
因为他的头发，他分头的方式。

370
00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:13.930
You're right.
你说得对。

371
00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:14.230
Yeah.
是啊。

372
00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.430
It's got the shrewd part.
那分头显得很精明。

373
00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:17.490
The shrewd part.
精明的分头。

374
00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:18.310
The shrewd part.
精明的分头。

375
00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:19.050
Absolutely.
绝对是。

376
00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:19.750
Yeah.
没错。

377
00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:23.350
Well, there's a lot of artistic interpretation with this mural.
嗯，这幅壁画有很多艺术解读的空间。

378
00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:24.910
Yes, there are.
确实如此。

379
00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.490
But anyway, big thanks to the LA Connection Comedy Theater.
总之，非常感谢洛杉矶联结喜剧剧院。

380
00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:30.530
Well, before we let you go, will you tell us about Sweeney Todd?
那么，在你离开之前，能跟我们聊聊《理发师陶德》吗？

381
00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:34.250
Are you going to be in Sweeney Todd until January 2024?
你会一直演《理发师陶德》到2024年1月吗？

382
00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:35.510
I am.
是的。

383
00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:36.250
Yes.
没错。

384
00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:43.610
So this is a role that I've loved ever since I was a little baritone that couldn't dance
这是一个我从小就喜欢的角色，那时我还是个不会跳舞的男中音，

385
00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:44.910
and thought that's the role for me.
心想这就是适合我的角色。

386
00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:49.010
I really love Sondheim's music.
我真的很喜欢桑德海姆的音乐。

387
00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:52.770
You know, we all, everybody who's in this cast has loved this show since we were little.
你知道，我们剧组里的每个人从小就喜欢这部剧。

388
00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:58.030
To have the opportunity to bring it to Broadway in a really large revival has been a dream.
能有机会在百老汇进行这样一场大型复排演出，一直以来都是我的梦想。

389
00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:02.950
So when Tommy Kail, our director, kind of said, hey, you know, if we're going to do this,
所以当我们的导演汤米·凯尔说，嘿，如果我们要做这件事，

390
00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:05.530
I really think we should think about like doing it.
我真的觉得我们应该认真考虑一下。

391
00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:10.330
You know, really diving in and saying this is what we're going to chisel for a year of work.
你知道，真正投入进去，说这就是我们未来一年要潜心打磨的作品。

392
00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:15.670
And obviously it's a big commitment, but it's one that's been super worth it for me to dive into.
显然这是一个巨大的承诺，但对我来说，投入其中是非常值得的。

393
00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:17.010
We're having an amazing time.
我们玩得很开心。

394
00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:18.670
And it's also funny.
而且它也很有趣。

395
00:22:18.850 --> 00:22:22.210
Like there's parts where the audience are just absolutely cracking up.
有些片段观众绝对会笑得前仰后合。

396
00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:23.650
There's dark humor in it.
里面有黑色幽默。

397
00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:27.870
The music is some of the most extraordinary music that I've ever heard in musical theater.
这音乐是我在音乐剧中听过最非凡的音乐之一。

398
00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:30.750
And it's a bloody, bloody good time.
而且这真是一段血腥又过瘾的时光。

399
