在6分32秒的时候，那句“祝你在那儿玩得开心”是他即兴发挥的吗？

877
00:42:37.970 --> 00:42:41.250
This cracks me up every time and I would love to know.
每次看到这儿我都笑得不行，我很想知道答案。

878
00:42:41.630 --> 00:42:43.510
Well, I looked it up.
嗯，我查了一下。

879
00:42:43.770 --> 00:42:45.170
It was not in the script.
剧本里并没有这句台词。

880
00:42:45.730 --> 00:42:48.930
It was also not in the script that Moe speeds away.
莫斯加速离开也不是剧本里写的。

881
00:42:49.530 --> 00:42:55.230
Instead, the script said he backs the car around the corner and then drives the car through a cornfield,
剧本里写的是他把车倒进拐角，然后开车穿过一片玉米地，

882
00:42:55.230 --> 00:42:57.310
mowing down a row of stalks.
撞倒了一排玉米秆。

883
00:42:57.430 --> 00:43:01.710
At a random spot, he stops, gets out, and leaves it.
在某个随机的地方，他停下车，走出来，然后把车丢在那儿。

884
00:43:02.370 --> 00:43:02.850
Amazing.
太绝了。

885
00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:06.630
It wasn't Mike Schur driving that car into that field, was it?
开车冲进那片地里的不是迈克·舒尔本人吧？

886
00:43:06.870 --> 00:43:12.350
I don't think it was him driving into the corn stalks, but I think it's him speeding away.
我觉得冲进玉米秆里的人不是他，但加速离开的那个人应该是他。

887
00:43:12.850 --> 00:43:13.210
Yeah.
是的。

888
00:43:13.550 --> 00:43:14.610
I mean, there's no cut.
我是说，镜头没有剪辑。

889
00:43:14.790 --> 00:43:16.690
He gets in the car and speeds away.
他上了车，然后加速离开了。

890
00:43:16.910 --> 00:43:21.130
But later, I don't think that's him going into the actual stalks.
但后来，我觉得冲进玉米秆里的那个人不是他。

891
00:43:21.190 --> 00:43:22.270
I was so curious.
我当时特别好奇。

892
00:43:22.870 --> 00:43:23.870
Kevin is going to arrive.
凯文要到了。

893
00:43:23.870 --> 00:43:25.250
He's rocking his toupee.
他戴着他的假发。

894
00:43:25.550 --> 00:43:26.590
Nice callback.
不错的呼应。

895
00:43:27.090 --> 00:43:29.490
Kelly and Aaron have their fascinators on.
凯利和亚伦戴着她们的装饰礼帽。

896
00:43:30.130 --> 00:43:33.990
And Dwight starts yelling everyone's name as they arrive.
德怀特开始在客人们到达时大声喊出每个人的名字。

897
00:43:34.830 --> 00:43:36.430
Jim has a talking head that says,
吉姆有个采访镜头说，

898
00:43:36.610 --> 00:43:38.870
Announcing guest's arrival is the height of decorum.
大声宣布客人的到来是礼仪的最高境界。

899
00:43:38.990 --> 00:43:41.190
The more volume, the more honor bestowed.
声音越大，给予的荣誉就越高。

900
00:43:41.390 --> 00:43:43.190
He's written this in his book, lady.
他把这些都写在他的书里了，女士。

901
00:43:43.410 --> 00:43:45.790
This is part of his book and Dwight is following the rules.
这是他书中的一部分，而德怀特正在遵守规则。

902
00:43:46.210 --> 00:43:48.850
You might have noticed that when Jim and Pam arrive,
你们可能注意到了，当吉姆和帕姆到达时，

903
00:43:49.170 --> 00:43:52.390
they are announced as Pamela James and P.P.
他们被介绍为帕梅拉·詹姆斯和P.P.

904
00:43:52.590 --> 00:43:52.970
Halpert.
哈珀特。

905
00:43:52.970 --> 00:43:55.930
This was a callback that was improvised by Rain.
这是一个由雷恩即兴发挥的梗。

906
00:43:56.330 --> 00:44:00.410
In the script, it simply said that he mumbles the baby's name.
剧本里只是简单写着他嘟囔了婴儿的名字。

907
00:44:00.550 --> 00:44:05.490
So he would have said, James, Pamela, and P.P.
所以他本该说的是，詹姆斯、帕梅拉和P.P.

908
00:44:05.770 --> 00:44:06.450
Halpert.
哈珀特。

909
00:44:07.470 --> 00:44:11.930
But if you remember, Dwight called their daughter pee-pee in search committee,
但如果你们还记得，德怀特在《搜寻委员会》那一集里管他们的女儿叫“尿尿（pee-pee）”，

910
00:44:12.090 --> 00:44:13.690
and Rainn Wilson called it back.
而雷恩·威尔森又把这个梗接上了。

911
00:44:14.070 --> 00:44:15.230
Nice, Rainn.
干得好，雷恩。

912
00:44:15.430 --> 00:44:19.750
Well, Oscar's annoyed by Andy's hovering, and Andy says to Oscar,
奥斯卡对安迪的徘徊感到恼火，安迪对奥斯卡说，

913
00:44:20.070 --> 00:44:21.850
I want everything to be nice.
我希望一切都好好的。

914
00:44:21.910 --> 00:44:22.990
That okay with you, Mabel?
你没意见吧，梅布尔？

915
00:44:23.570 --> 00:44:26.650
Mabel, Mabel, if you're able, keep your elbows off the table.
梅布尔，梅布尔，如果你能做到，就把你的手肘从桌子上拿开。

916
00:44:27.230 --> 00:44:27.750
Hmm.
嗯。

917
00:44:28.130 --> 00:44:29.330
This made me curious.
这让我很好奇。

918
00:44:29.670 --> 00:44:32.590
Were there other Andy etiquette sayings in the shooting draft?
拍摄剧本里还有其他安迪的礼仪格言吗？

919
00:44:32.730 --> 00:44:33.510
And Jenna, there were.
珍娜，还真有。

920
00:44:33.870 --> 00:44:34.230
Really?
真的吗？

921
00:44:34.830 --> 00:44:35.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

922
00:44:35.310 --> 00:44:37.410
This one's in deleted scenes.
这一段在删减片段里。

923
00:44:37.750 --> 00:44:42.390
Kevin is taking way too many appetizers, and Andy walks up to him and says,
凯文拿了太多的开胃菜，安迪走过去对他说，

924
00:44:42.590 --> 00:44:47.710
Kevin, this totally reminds me of this really lame, useful saying I learned as a kid.
凯文，这完全让我想起了我小时候学过的一句很烂但很有用的格言。

925
00:44:48.290 --> 00:44:52.030
What's the difference between hors d'oeuvres and the animals on Noah's Ark?
开胃菜和诺亚方舟上的动物有什么区别？

926
00:44:52.290 --> 00:44:55.590
With hors d'oeuvres, we only take one at a time.
对于开胃菜，我们一次只拿一个。

927
00:44:56.250 --> 00:44:57.270
Oh, amazing.
哦，太棒了。

928
00:44:59.430 --> 00:45:01.590
So many rules in Andy's life.
安迪的生活里有太多规矩了。

929
00:45:01.850 --> 00:45:03.090
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

930
00:45:03.090 --> 00:45:06.370
The people Andy has been waiting for have arrived.
安迪一直在等的人到了。

931
00:45:06.590 --> 00:45:12.450
Dwight very loudly announces the arrival of Walter and Ellen Bernard.
德怀特非常大声地宣布了沃尔特和艾伦·伯纳德的到来。

932
00:45:13.490 --> 00:45:20.910
When Rain is Dwight yelled their names, I thought the actress that played Ellen's reaction was so great.
当雷恩饰演的德怀特大喊他们的名字时，我觉得饰演艾伦的那位女演员的反应太棒了。

933
00:45:21.170 --> 00:45:21.590
So good.
太好了。

934
00:45:22.010 --> 00:45:23.490
So thrown off.
完全被搞懵了。

935
00:45:23.610 --> 00:45:24.670
Like, what is happening?
就像是，这到底是怎么回事？

936
00:45:25.330 --> 00:45:25.690
Yes.
是的。

937
00:45:26.030 --> 00:45:29.570
Dee Wallace is who played Andy's mom, Ellen.
迪·华莱士饰演了安迪的妈妈艾伦。

938
00:45:30.030 --> 00:45:34.610
Steve Burgess worked with her before and was so excited to have her back on the show.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯以前和她合作过，非常高兴能让她回到剧组。

939
00:45:34.610 --> 00:45:42.870
Angela, I know Dee, not personally, but because she has starred in so many classic horror filMs.
安吉拉，我认识迪，不是私下认识，是因为她主演过太多经典恐怖片了。

940
00:45:43.050 --> 00:45:44.870
She is like a horror queen.
她简直是恐怖片女王。

941
00:45:45.070 --> 00:45:46.570
I love her.
我爱死她了。

942
00:45:46.730 --> 00:45:47.530
Oh, I didn't know.
哦，我不知道。

943
00:45:47.670 --> 00:45:50.650
She was in the original 1977 The Hills Have Eyes.
她出演了1977年的原版《隔山有眼》。

944
00:45:50.890 --> 00:45:55.950
She was in The Howling, Cujo, Critters, Halloween, Death House.
她还演过《破胆三次》、《狂犬惊魂》、《魔精》、《月光光心慌慌》、《死亡屋》。

945
00:45:56.470 --> 00:45:59.990
She is probably most famous for playing the mom in E.T.
她最出名的角色大概是《E.T.外星人》里的妈妈。

946
00:46:00.590 --> 00:46:00.950
Yes.
是的。

947
00:46:01.170 --> 00:46:01.590
Yes.
没错。

948
00:46:01.730 --> 00:46:02.810
That's how I know Dee.
我就是通过这些认识迪的。

949
00:46:03.030 --> 00:46:03.290
Yes.
是的。

950
00:46:03.510 --> 00:46:04.550
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

951
00:46:04.690 --> 00:46:05.710
And also Cujo.
还有《狂犬惊魂》。

952
00:46:05.850 --> 00:46:07.610
I remember Cujo scared the crap out of me.
我记得《狂犬惊魂》把我吓得半死。

953
00:46:07.750 --> 00:46:08.130
Yes.
没错。

954
00:46:08.370 --> 00:46:13.750
She said in an interview with Entertainment Tonight that she absolutely loves doing horror roles.
她在接受《娱乐今晚》采访时说，她非常喜欢演恐怖片角色。

955
00:46:13.910 --> 00:46:15.930
And this was, I thought, really funny.
我觉得这一点特别有趣。

956
00:46:16.170 --> 00:46:21.890
She said that if she had to have a career, like, just in comedy or something, it would just be so boring.
她说如果她的职业生涯只能演喜剧之类的，那会非常无聊。

957
00:46:22.810 --> 00:46:26.650
Which is so funny because she is so good in this episode.
这很有趣，因为她在这一集里的表现太棒了。

958
00:46:27.150 --> 00:46:27.310
Yeah.
是啊。

959
00:46:27.310 --> 00:46:30.810
Everything about her is so subtle, and I couldn't take my eyes off her.
她的一切都处理得非常细腻，我目不转睛。

960
00:46:30.890 --> 00:46:31.870
I thought she was fantastic.
我觉得她演得太好了。

961
00:46:32.610 --> 00:46:36.650
And then Stephen Collins is who played Walter Sr.
还有饰演老沃尔特的斯蒂芬·柯林斯。

962
00:46:37.090 --> 00:46:42.190
He is very famous for playing the dad on Seventh Heaven, which he was on for 11 seasons.
他因在《七重天》中饰演父亲而闻名，他在那部剧里演了11季。

963
00:46:42.810 --> 00:46:44.690
I have never seen Seventh Heaven.
我从没看过《七重天》。

964
00:46:44.890 --> 00:46:45.990
I had not either.
我也没看过。

965
00:46:46.230 --> 00:46:47.110
I missed it.
我错过了。

966
00:46:47.450 --> 00:46:48.810
But here is the thing.
但重点是。

967
00:46:48.810 --> 00:46:55.990
I guess I need to say, you might be aware of some news that came out about Stephen in 2014.
我想我得说，你可能听说过2014年关于斯蒂芬的一些新闻。

968
00:46:55.990 --> 00:46:58.310
I don't know how to say this delicately.
我不知道该怎么委婉地说。

969
00:46:58.310 --> 00:47:01.710
I know a lot of people listen to the podcast with their kids.
我知道很多人会和孩子一起听这个播客。

970
00:47:02.050 --> 00:47:02.390
Yes.
是的。

971
00:47:02.630 --> 00:47:12.690
So let me just say that in 2014, Stephen came forward and admitted to some pretty disturbing behavior in his paSt.
所以我只想说，2014年，斯蒂芬主动承认了他过去一些相当令人不安的行为。

972
00:47:13.290 --> 00:47:16.350
If you Google him, it's the very first thing that comes up.
如果你去谷歌搜索他，最先跳出来的就是这些。

973
00:47:16.350 --> 00:47:23.150
I don't want to maybe get into too many details here, but I did just want to mention that.
我不想在这里深入讨论细节，但我确实想提一下。

974
00:47:23.430 --> 00:47:26.310
It was long after we had filmed with him.
那是在我们和他拍完戏很久之后的事了。

975
00:47:26.670 --> 00:47:29.590
But yeah, it's upsetting.
但确实，这很令人难过。

976
00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:30.770
Okay.
好吧。

977
00:47:31.170 --> 00:47:32.430
I'll leave it at that.
我就说到这儿吧。

978
00:47:32.870 --> 00:47:33.330
Okay.
好的。

979
00:47:33.330 --> 00:47:41.310
We also, Angela, got a fan mail flurry of people writing in to point out that these are not the people we met at Toby's Going Away Party.
安吉拉，我们还收到了一大堆粉丝来信，指出这些人并不是我们在托比欢送会上见到的那些人。

980
00:47:41.670 --> 00:47:42.130
Right.
没错。

981
00:47:42.310 --> 00:47:44.250
When Andy proposes to Angela.
就是安迪向安吉拉求婚的时候。

982
00:47:44.530 --> 00:47:45.050
Yes.
是的。

983
00:47:45.090 --> 00:47:48.450
It cuts to his parents and they are not the same actors.
镜头切到他父母时，演员换人了。

984
00:47:48.730 --> 00:47:50.650
They also do not have the same names.
他们的名字也不一样了。

985
00:47:50.650 --> 00:47:56.190
They are introduced as Ellen and Andrew Bernard, not Ellen and Walter Bernard.
他们被介绍为艾伦和安德鲁·伯纳德，而不是艾伦和沃尔特·伯纳德。

986
00:47:56.190 --> 00:48:04.630
Now, you know, we have the show Bible where you have everyone's character and their history and their origin story.
你知道，我们有剧集设定集，里面记录了每个角色的背景和起源故事。

987
00:48:04.810 --> 00:48:05.650
How did this happen?
这是怎么回事呢？

988
00:48:06.050 --> 00:48:17.250
Well, after we did Goodbye, Toby, we had this very funny joke in a later episode where Andy says that his original name was Walter, that he was named after his dad.
嗯，在拍完《再见，托比》之后，我们在后面的一集里加了个很有趣的梗，安迪说他原本叫沃尔特，是随他父亲的名字。

989
00:48:17.490 --> 00:48:17.770
Yeah.
是啊。

990
00:48:17.970 --> 00:48:24.010
But then later when his younger brother was born, they renamed him Andy and then called his little brother Walter Jr.
但后来他弟弟出生时，他们把他改名叫安迪，然后叫他弟弟小沃尔特。

991
00:48:24.950 --> 00:48:25.390
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

992
00:48:25.390 --> 00:48:32.370
So that was a joke that kind of went against that Goodbye, Toby moment, but it was so funny.
所以那个笑话有点违背了《再见，托比》里的设定，但真的太好笑了。

993
00:48:32.750 --> 00:48:36.450
Sometimes when something was really funny to them, they would just go against the show Bible.
有时候，如果某个点子对他们来说特别好笑，他们就会无视设定集。

994
00:48:36.650 --> 00:48:38.730
They were like, comedy first, show Bible later.
他们觉得喜剧优先，设定集靠后。

995
00:48:38.970 --> 00:48:43.910
But I want to share a very interesting fan theory sent in by Eva S.
但我想要分享一个由来自伊利诺伊州奥罗拉的伊娃·S发来的非常有趣的粉丝理论。

996
00:48:44.070 --> 00:48:44.990
from Aurora, Illinois.
来自伊利诺伊州奥罗拉。

997
00:48:45.310 --> 00:48:47.050
I absolutely adored it.
我简直太喜欢这个理论了。

998
00:48:47.290 --> 00:48:47.910
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

999
00:48:48.210 --> 00:48:49.070
Eva says,
伊娃说，

1000
00:49:06.610 --> 00:49:16.630
And this is why he's so attached to his gam-gam, who we will meet later.
这就是为什么他那么依恋他的奶奶，我们之后会见到她。

1001
00:49:16.630 --> 00:49:23.190
When Andy was still a kid, his father had an affair with his secretary, as noted in Secretary's Day.
安迪小时候，他父亲曾与秘书有过一段婚外情，这在《秘书节》那一集中提到过。

1002
00:49:24.010 --> 00:49:28.890
Separating from Ellen and setting up a separate household with the secretary and her kids.
父亲与艾伦分居，并与秘书及其孩子们另组了家庭。

1003
00:49:29.390 --> 00:49:35.110
Even though Walter and the secretary were never officially married, this is who Andy means when he says, quote,
尽管沃尔特和那位秘书从未正式结婚，但安迪说那句话时指的就是他们，引用如下：

1004
00:49:35.330 --> 00:49:37.990
If it wasn't for secretaries, I wouldn't have a stepmom.
如果不是因为秘书，我就不会有继母了。

1005
00:49:38.550 --> 00:49:40.990
Andy got attached to her and her kids.
安迪和她以及她的孩子们产生了深厚的感情。

1006
00:49:40.990 --> 00:49:44.590
Even years later, he will refer to them as his brothers and sister.
即使多年以后，他仍会称呼他们为他的兄弟姐妹。

1007
00:49:44.730 --> 00:49:49.730
And this is why he says he's wearing his sister's old field hockey skirt in St. Patrick's Day.
这就是为什么他在《圣帕特里克节》里说他穿着他姐姐旧的曲棍球裙。

1008
00:49:50.170 --> 00:49:56.110
And why he talks about doing puzzles with his brothers, plural, when we're out sailing in PDA.
也是为什么我们在《公开示爱》那集去航海时，他会说和他的兄弟们（复数）一起玩拼图。

1009
00:49:56.690 --> 00:49:57.590
Eva goes on.
伊娃继续说道。

1010
00:49:57.950 --> 00:49:58.650
Walter Sr.
老沃尔特

1011
00:49:58.690 --> 00:50:03.750
and Ellen end up going to the Breakers in Newport, Connecticut, where they decide not to get divorced.
和艾伦最终去了康涅狄格州纽波特的布雷克斯酒店，在那里他们决定不离婚。

1012
00:50:03.790 --> 00:50:05.390
Remember, that was from weight loss.
记住，那是减肥带来的结果。

1013
00:50:05.930 --> 00:50:07.110
So Walter Sr.
所以老沃尔特

1014
00:50:07.150 --> 00:50:12.530
broke up with the secretary, putting an end to Andy's stepfamily, but they stayed in his heart.
与秘书分手了，结束了安迪的继亲家庭，但他们依然留在他的心里。

1015
00:50:12.730 --> 00:50:15.770
That's why he still thinks of them as his real brothers and sister.
这就是为什么他仍然把他们当作自己真正的兄弟姐妹。

1016
00:50:16.210 --> 00:50:21.170
But why did we see Andrew and Ellen Bernard at Toby's going away party?
但为什么我们在托比的欢送会上看到了安德鲁和艾伦·伯纳德？

1017
00:50:21.590 --> 00:50:28.810
Because Andy, who needs to make himself look good, actually hired two community theater performers to pose at his parents
因为安迪为了让自己看起来体面，雇了两名社区剧院的演员来扮演他的父母，

1018
00:50:28.810 --> 00:50:31.810
and act proud of him to impress his co-workers and Angela.
并假装为他感到骄傲，以此给他的同事和安吉拉留下深刻印象。

1019
00:50:32.050 --> 00:50:38.670
And then he named his pretend father, Andrew, so that he could be his father's namesake at laSt.
然后他给假父亲取名安德鲁，这样他终于可以成为父亲的同名者了。

1020
00:50:39.010 --> 00:50:39.490
Oh.
哦。

1021
00:50:40.650 --> 00:50:45.910
So those are all of her theories that bring together all of these inconsistencies.
所以这些就是她将所有这些前后矛盾之处串联起来的理论。

1022
00:50:46.330 --> 00:50:48.510
Eva, I think you knocked it out of the park.
伊娃，我觉得你分析得太精彩了。

1023
00:50:48.730 --> 00:50:50.450
That all made it make sense for me.
这让我一切都想通了。

1024
00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:53.270
Eva, you're doing our writers a great service.
伊娃，你为我们的编剧帮了大忙。

1025
00:50:53.510 --> 00:50:54.250
Mm-hmm, you are.
嗯哼，确实如此。

1026
00:50:54.270 --> 00:50:57.310
By tying together all of those loose ends, I thought it was fantastic.
把所有这些零散的线索串联起来，我觉得太棒了。

1027
00:50:58.050 --> 00:51:01.890
Well, we're going to find out that Andy's parents don't have much time to be at the garden party
好吧，我们将会发现安迪的父母在花园派对上待的时间并不多，

1028
00:51:01.890 --> 00:51:07.510
because they have theater tickets to see Moneyball with Andy's brother, who shows up.
因为他们买了剧院票，要和安迪随后出现的兄弟一起去看《点球成金》。

1029
00:51:07.790 --> 00:51:09.650
His Bronard is in attendance.
他的兄弟伯纳德出席了。

1030
00:51:10.550 --> 00:51:11.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1031
00:51:11.450 --> 00:51:12.490
That was a shock.
那真是个惊喜。

1032
00:51:12.490 --> 00:51:13.910
We didn't hear him announced.
我们没听到有人宣布他到场。

1033
00:51:14.530 --> 00:51:15.010
No.
没有。

1034
00:51:15.350 --> 00:51:20.130
I think we should take a break because things are really going to start happening at this party.
我想我们该休息一下了，因为派对上接下来要发生大事了。

1035
00:51:20.330 --> 00:51:21.830
Yes, now that Walter Jr.
是的，现在小沃尔特

1036
00:51:22.090 --> 00:51:24.190
has arrived, things are going to get interesting.
已经到了，事情要变得有趣了。

1037
00:51:24.530 --> 00:51:25.430
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1038
00:51:34.630 --> 00:51:38.750
We are back, and one of my favorite moments in this whole episode happens.
我们回来了，这一集中我最喜欢的时刻之一即将发生。

1039
00:51:39.450 --> 00:51:43.550
A crow is going to fly and steal Erin's hat off of her head.
一只乌鸦飞过来，从艾琳头上抢走了她的帽子。

1040
00:51:43.750 --> 00:51:43.950
Yeah.
没错。

1041
00:51:44.110 --> 00:51:46.610
I thought Ellie's reaction was so perfect.
我觉得艾莉的反应太完美了。

1042
00:51:47.690 --> 00:51:49.230
I loved all of this.
我喜欢这一切。

1043
00:51:49.330 --> 00:51:50.770
You know me and my birds, lady.
你了解我和我的鸟，女士。

1044
00:51:50.930 --> 00:51:56.150
I was like, if a bird took my hat off my head, I would be like, this is the coolest moment.
我就想，如果有一只鸟从我头上拿走帽子，我会觉得，这简直太酷了。

1045
00:51:56.150 --> 00:51:56.850
What's happening?
发生了什么？

1046
00:51:58.810 --> 00:52:01.850
We got a fan question about this moment from Megan T.
我们收到了来自爱荷华州得梅因的梅根·T关于这一时刻的粉丝提问，她问：

1047
00:52:01.990 --> 00:52:03.870
in Des Moines, Iowa, who asked,
我必须知道关于那只鸟抢走艾琳帽子的所有细节。

1048
00:52:04.130 --> 00:52:08.250
I have to know all the details about the bird taking Erin's hat.
梅根和你一样，安吉拉。

1049
00:52:08.530 --> 00:52:09.930
Megan is like you, Angela.
梅根想知道这花了多少钱，训练那只鸟花了多长时间，

1050
00:52:10.530 --> 00:52:14.590
Megan would like to know how much did it cost, how long did it take to train the bird,
梅根想知道这花了多少钱，训练那只鸟花了多长时间，

1051
00:52:14.590 --> 00:52:19.750
and how many takes did it take, and how did Ellie Kemper feel about it because it would freak me out?
拍了多少次才过？艾莉·坎伯当时是什么感觉？因为要是我的话肯定会吓坏的。

1052
00:52:20.030 --> 00:52:21.570
Oh, maybe she's not like you.
噢，也许她不像你这样。

1053
00:52:21.570 --> 00:52:23.770
It sounds like Megan would be freaked out.
听起来梅根确实会被吓到。

1054
00:52:23.970 --> 00:52:26.750
I know, but Megan, it'd also be kind of cool, right?
我知道，但梅根，这其实也挺酷的，对吧？

1055
00:52:26.930 --> 00:52:27.950
Like, it'd be kind of cool.
就是说，这其实挺酷的。

1056
00:52:28.330 --> 00:52:32.930
Well, Megan, I reached out to Steve Burgess to find out how we did this,
好吧，梅根，我联系了史蒂夫·伯吉斯去了解我们是怎么拍这一幕的，

1057
00:52:32.970 --> 00:52:37.970
and I'm sorry to disappoint you, but this hat gag was totally fake.
很抱歉要让你失望了，这个帽子梗完全是假的。

1058
00:52:38.150 --> 00:52:44.010
He said that the special effects team used a fishing pole and some, like, you know,
他说特效团队用了一根钓鱼竿和一些，你知道的，

1059
00:52:44.090 --> 00:52:47.330
invisible wire to yank the hat off of Ellie's head.
隐形钢丝把帽子从艾莉头上拽了下来。

1060
00:52:47.330 --> 00:52:52.010
She's just reacting to that, and they added the crow later as special effects.
她只是在对那个做出反应，乌鸦是后来用特效加上去的。

1061
00:52:52.410 --> 00:52:54.630
There was no trained crow at all.
根本就没有受过训练的乌鸦。

1062
00:52:55.130 --> 00:52:57.050
That's how well Ellie sold it.
艾莉演得太逼真了。

1063
00:52:57.110 --> 00:52:57.770
For sure.
确实。

1064
00:52:58.330 --> 00:53:03.190
Now we're going to have a bit that is 100% stolen from the movie Bridesmaids,
现在我们要来一段百分之百抄袭自电影《伴娘》的桥段，

1065
00:53:03.230 --> 00:53:04.330
where Walter Jr.
在那部电影里，小沃尔特

1066
00:53:04.830 --> 00:53:09.390
introduces himself to Jim and then thinks that Meredith is his wife Pam,
向吉姆做了自我介绍，然后以为梅雷迪思是他妻子帕姆，

1067
00:53:09.590 --> 00:53:11.430
and this joke is going to get repeated.
这个笑话会被反复使用。

1068
00:53:12.050 --> 00:53:14.670
This is one of my favorite bits from the movie Bridesmaids.
这是我最喜欢的《伴娘》里的桥段之一。

1069
00:53:14.670 --> 00:53:17.630
This happens to Kristen Wiig's character over and over again.
克里斯汀·韦格饰演的角色在电影里反复遭遇这种事。

1070
00:53:18.270 --> 00:53:22.210
Well, Dwight is now going to perform a dance routine with the waitress,
好了，现在德怀特要和女服务员跳一段舞，

1071
00:53:22.210 --> 00:53:28.270
and then after this, there would have been another scene of Dwight making a giant ice sculpture.
在这之后，原本还有一场德怀特制作巨型冰雕的戏。

1072
00:53:28.590 --> 00:53:29.950
It's in Deleted Scenes.
在删减片段里有。

1073
00:53:30.090 --> 00:53:31.210
It's also in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本里也有。

1074
00:53:31.450 --> 00:53:37.690
Dwight has a chainsaw and a huge block of ice, and he's really just carving away,
德怀特拿着电锯和一大块冰，他真的很卖力地在雕刻，

1075
00:53:37.830 --> 00:53:41.410
and what he ends up with is just something that looks like a blob.
但他最后雕出来的东西看起来就像一团糊状物。

1076
00:53:41.410 --> 00:53:43.050
I remember this.
我记得这个。

1077
00:53:43.530 --> 00:53:45.970
He rolls it out, and he's really proud of it, and he says,
他把它推出来，还引以为傲，他说，

1078
00:53:46.110 --> 00:53:49.370
I give you the Alamo, but it just looks like a blob.
“我向你们展示阿拉莫”，但它看起来就是一团糊状物。

1079
00:53:51.210 --> 00:53:54.510
And then there would have been a Jim talking head where Jim would have said,
然后原本还有一段吉姆的采访镜头，吉姆会说，

1080
00:53:54.970 --> 00:54:01.010
Chapter 7, the host should always present something spectacular to draw the eye of the guests.
“第七章，主人应该总是展示一些壮观的东西来吸引客人的目光。”

1081
00:54:01.870 --> 00:54:03.650
So we're at Chapter 7 now.
所以我们现在讲到第七章了。

1082
00:54:04.370 --> 00:54:07.850
Well, Moe's is still managing all the cars in the parking lot.
莫斯还在管理停车场里所有的车。

1083
00:54:07.850 --> 00:54:11.590
He's parked them so close together that he exits through the sunroof.
他把车停得太近了，只能从天窗钻出来。

1084
00:54:12.010 --> 00:54:14.990
And we got a fan catch from Michaela G.
我们收到了一位粉丝米凯拉·G的发现，

1085
00:54:15.310 --> 00:54:16.770
in Wisconsin, who said,
来自威斯康星州，她说，

1086
00:54:16.970 --> 00:54:20.830
At 9 minutes and 51 seconds, when Moe's is parking all of the cars in the field,
在9分51秒时，当莫斯在田野里停放所有车辆时，

1087
00:54:20.970 --> 00:54:25.750
there are these bright green colored pieces of paper on all the vehicle's windshields.
所有车的挡风玻璃上都有这种亮绿色的纸片。

1088
00:54:26.330 --> 00:54:27.470
What are they?
那是什么？

1089
00:54:27.670 --> 00:54:30.570
Is there a deleted scene that explains what they are?
有没有删减片段解释它们是什么？

1090
00:54:31.210 --> 00:54:32.950
Michaela, I noticed these as well.
米凯拉，我也注意到了。

1091
00:54:33.110 --> 00:54:33.410
Angela?
安吉拉？

1092
00:54:37.850 --> 00:54:40.790
Very beginning of the episode when they're in the conference room.
在剧集刚开始他们在会议室的时候。

1093
00:54:41.050 --> 00:54:42.590
Everyone has been handed out.
每个人都发到了。

1094
00:54:42.630 --> 00:54:46.450
It looks like it says parking for Shroop Farms, like a green flyer.
看起来上面写着“施鲁特农场停车证”，像是一张绿色传单。

1095
00:54:46.910 --> 00:54:47.210
Yes.
没错。

1096
00:54:47.450 --> 00:54:50.330
Dwight has a line that was cut where he says,
德怀特有一句被剪掉的台词，他说，

1097
00:54:51.310 --> 00:54:52.130
Rip it in thirds.
“把它撕成三份。”

1098
00:54:52.450 --> 00:54:56.710
One is the map, one is your invitation, and the last is your parking pass.
“一份是地图，一份是邀请函，最后一份是停车证。”

1099
00:54:57.010 --> 00:54:58.370
Just put it on your dashboard.
“把它放在仪表盘上就行了。”

1100
00:54:58.790 --> 00:55:00.210
So good catch, Michaela?
所以，发现得好，米凯拉。

1101
00:55:00.810 --> 00:55:01.830
Very good catch.
抓得真准。

1102
00:55:01.830 --> 00:55:07.130
Dwight is now going to announce the arrival of Robert California.
德怀特现在要宣布罗伯特·加利福尼亚的到来了。

1103
00:55:08.490 --> 00:55:10.950
He like rolls his R for so long.
他卷舌音发得好长。

1104
00:55:11.170 --> 00:55:14.670
In the shooting draft, Jenna, right after Robert arrives,
在拍摄剧本里，珍娜，就在罗伯特到达之后，

1105
00:55:15.400 --> 00:55:18.170
in true Robert California dramatic fashion,
以罗伯特·加利福尼亚那种典型的戏剧性方式，

1106
00:55:18.170 --> 00:55:21.150
he goes and he stands by a tractor.
他走过去站在了一台拖拉机旁边。

1107
00:55:21.370 --> 00:55:23.790
He gazes out around the farm,
他凝视着农场四周，

1108
00:55:23.790 --> 00:55:27.410
and then he turns to camera, and he says this.
然后转向镜头，说了这段话。

1109
00:55:27.490 --> 00:55:28.650
I have the clip.
我有这段片段。

1110
00:55:28.810 --> 00:55:29.290
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1111
00:55:30.430 --> 00:55:35.990
So much depends upon a red wheelbarrow glazed with rainwater beside the white chickens.
一切都取决于那辆红色的手推车，上面沾着雨水，停在白色的鸡群旁。

1112
00:55:38.090 --> 00:55:39.690
William Carlos WilliaMs.
威廉·卡洛斯·威廉斯。

1113
00:55:41.090 --> 00:55:41.730
Hmm.
嗯。

1114
00:55:42.630 --> 00:55:43.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1115
00:55:43.330 --> 00:55:43.790
Beautiful.
太美了。

1116
00:55:44.310 --> 00:55:46.490
And then he dramatically walks away.
然后他戏剧性地走开了。

1117
00:55:46.850 --> 00:55:49.050
I looked up William Carlos WilliaMs.
我查了一下威廉·卡洛斯·威廉斯。

1118
00:55:49.350 --> 00:55:50.830
According to the Poetry Foundation,
根据诗歌基金会的说法，

1119
00:55:51.130 --> 00:55:55.570
he was a medical doctor, poet, novelist, essayist, and playwright.
他是一位医生、诗人、小说家、散文家和剧作家。

1120
00:55:55.850 --> 00:55:58.810
Williams was a leading poet of the imaginist movement
威廉斯是意象派运动的领军诗人，

1121
00:55:58.810 --> 00:56:01.390
and often wrote of American subjects and themes.
经常描写美国题材和主题。

1122
00:56:01.790 --> 00:56:04.650
Though his career was initially overshadowed by other poets,
虽然他的职业生涯最初被其他诗人掩盖了光芒，

1123
00:56:04.830 --> 00:56:09.730
he became an inspiration to the beat generation of the 1950s and 60s.
但他成为了五六十年代“垮掉的一代”的灵感来源。

1124
00:56:09.850 --> 00:56:13.210
He was known as an experimenter, an innovator,
他被称为实验者、创新者，

1125
00:56:13.410 --> 00:56:15.810
a revolutionary figure in American poetry.
是美国诗坛的一位革命性人物。

1126
00:56:16.090 --> 00:56:16.490
Hmm.
嗯。

1127
00:56:16.850 --> 00:56:18.050
It's very random.
这太随机了。

1128
00:56:18.350 --> 00:56:21.830
I wonder which of our writers is a poetry fan and knew about him.
我很好奇我们哪位编剧是诗歌爱好者，还了解他。

1129
00:56:22.340 --> 00:56:23.010
I know.
我也这么想。

1130
00:56:23.410 --> 00:56:28.490
Because that's a pretty specific poet and line to have Robert California quote.
因为让罗伯特·加利福尼亚引用这位诗人的诗句，确实非常特别。

1131
00:56:28.690 --> 00:56:29.050
I know.
我知道。

1132
00:56:29.050 --> 00:56:31.930
Very perfect for the character of Robert California as well.
而且也非常符合罗伯特·加利福尼亚这个角色。

1133
00:56:32.270 --> 00:56:33.470
I thought so too.
我也这么认为。

1134
00:56:33.470 --> 00:56:34.770
And it's super dramatic.
而且超级戏剧化。

1135
00:56:34.770 --> 00:56:38.450
And I kind of wish it had stayed in because it's so random and bizarre.
我倒有点希望这段戏能保留下来，因为它太随机、太离奇了。

1136
00:56:38.950 --> 00:56:41.570
Well, Robert has brought not the marmalade.
好吧，罗伯特带来的不是果酱。

1137
00:56:42.050 --> 00:56:42.590
No.
没错。

1138
00:56:42.790 --> 00:56:44.410
He brought the basil plant.
他带来的是一盆罗勒。

1139
00:56:44.930 --> 00:56:46.830
Which he was going to bring all along.
那是他本来就打算带来的。

1140
00:56:47.630 --> 00:56:50.190
We're going to see Kevin and Ryan now on the seesaw.
我们现在要看凯文和瑞安在跷跷板上的戏了。

1141
00:56:50.330 --> 00:56:51.810
It's not going so well for Ryan.
瑞安的情况不太妙。

1142
00:56:52.230 --> 00:56:52.610
No.
确实。

1143
00:56:52.750 --> 00:56:54.430
He's the one stuck up in the air there.
他就是那个被悬在半空中的人。

1144
00:56:54.770 --> 00:56:57.430
And then there would have been a scene, Jenna, here,
然后本来还有一场戏，珍娜，就在这儿，

1145
00:56:57.670 --> 00:57:01.230
between Angela and Pam that comes before the toaSt.
发生在安吉拉和帕姆之间，在祝酒之前。

1146
00:57:01.450 --> 00:57:03.130
It is packed with sass.
那场戏充满了刻薄。

1147
00:57:03.350 --> 00:57:04.570
So much sass.
太刻薄了。

1148
00:57:05.010 --> 00:57:09.370
It's the scene we shot inside, partially so you could cool off.
那是我们在室内拍的戏，部分原因是为了让你凉快一下。

1149
00:57:09.450 --> 00:57:09.830
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1150
00:57:10.210 --> 00:57:12.970
Because it was so hot and they were worried about you being outside.
因为当时太热了，他们担心你在外面会受不了。

1151
00:57:13.590 --> 00:57:15.830
But yeah, I think we have to hear this scene.
不过说真的，我觉得我们得听听这一场戏。

1152
00:57:15.830 --> 00:57:17.970
It was set up in the shooting draft like this.
拍摄剧本里是这样设定的。

1153
00:57:18.510 --> 00:57:20.850
Interior Schrute Farms, main house.
内景，舒鲁特农场，主屋。

1154
00:57:21.190 --> 00:57:23.990
Pam comes down the stairs holding a baby monitor.
帕姆拿着婴儿监视器走下楼梯。

1155
00:57:24.470 --> 00:57:26.450
Angela is sitting in the living room.
安吉拉坐在客厅里。

1156
00:57:26.730 --> 00:57:28.590
I'm titling the scene, Jenna.
我正在给这场戏加标题，珍娜。

1157
00:57:28.990 --> 00:57:30.570
And that is that.
事情就是这样。

1158
00:57:30.990 --> 00:57:31.950
Let's hear it.
我们来听听看。

1159
00:57:33.570 --> 00:57:34.950
Little Cece asleep?
小西西睡着了吗？

1160
00:57:35.310 --> 00:57:36.710
Yeah, she just went down.
嗯，刚睡下。

1161
00:57:37.090 --> 00:57:38.830
Such a precious little angel.
