1309
01:04:29.290 --> 01:04:35.610
Well, Andy is going to take control of things and he is going to suggest that he and his father sing a duet.
好吧，安迪打算掌控局面，他提议和父亲合唱一首歌。

1310
01:04:36.270 --> 01:04:38.710
He's going to get out his guitar and start playing.
他要拿出吉他开始弹奏。

1311
01:04:39.290 --> 01:04:41.370
And his dad has a lot of comments.
而他爸爸有很多意见。

1312
01:04:42.370 --> 01:04:43.550
It's the wrong key.
调子不对。

1313
01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:45.930
He just constantly stops him.
他一直在打断他。

1314
01:04:46.050 --> 01:04:46.210
Yes.
是的。

1315
01:04:46.210 --> 01:04:52.890
And then when they do finally start singing, my heart broke for Andy because Andy starts to do his Andy thing because he does his voice.
当他们终于开始唱的时候，我为安迪感到心碎，因为安迪开始做他那一套，用他那种独特的嗓音。

1316
01:04:53.090 --> 01:04:53.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1317
01:04:53.350 --> 01:04:54.530
He does his Andy voice.
他用他那标志性的安迪嗓音。

1318
01:04:55.270 --> 01:04:58.390
That is not meshing at all with his dad's voice.
那和他爸爸的嗓音完全不搭。

1319
01:04:58.910 --> 01:05:00.490
And his dad's going to stop it.
他爸爸肯定会叫停的。

1320
01:05:00.490 --> 01:05:11.710
His dad is going to stop it and call up Walter Jr., who, as we all know, is played by a man who has one of the most beautiful voices to grace this planet.
他爸爸会叫停，然后叫来小沃尔特，众所周知，扮演这个角色的演员拥有这颗星球上最美妙的嗓音之一。

1321
01:05:11.710 --> 01:05:14.350
But Josh Groban, oh my gosh.
但是乔什·格罗班，天哪。

1322
01:05:14.690 --> 01:05:19.810
We actually got a fan comment from Marissa Kay in Illinois who said,
我们确实收到了一条来自伊利诺伊州玛丽莎·凯的粉丝评论，她说：

1323
01:05:19.810 --> 01:05:23.770
I absolutely loved that they picked Josh Groban to be Andy's brother.
我非常喜欢他们选了乔什·格罗班来演安迪的弟弟。

1324
01:05:24.010 --> 01:05:27.590
And I thought it was tragically hilarious to have Walter Jr.
我觉得让小沃尔特唱歌明显比安迪好听，这简直是悲剧性的搞笑，

1325
01:05:27.650 --> 01:05:32.430
be a noticeably better singer than Andy because Andy loves to sing so much.
因为安迪是那么热爱唱歌。

1326
01:05:32.430 --> 01:05:36.390
There are so many layers to this family and their dynamic.
这个家庭及其成员间的互动有着太多的层次。

1327
01:05:36.650 --> 01:05:37.190
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1328
01:05:37.490 --> 01:05:41.250
I know people talk about Scott's Tots as being the cringiest episode.
我知道人们常说《斯科特的托儿所》是最让人尴尬的一集。

1329
01:05:41.690 --> 01:05:53.490
I found this episode and particularly this scene and the scenes to follow with Andy trying to impress his dad and never getting anywhere to be so incredibly uncomfortable to watch.
但我发现这一集，尤其是这一幕，以及随后安迪试图讨好父亲却屡屡碰壁的场景，看起来真是让人极其不适。

1330
01:05:53.650 --> 01:05:56.070
And then there is no resolution.
而且最后也没有得到解决。

1331
01:05:56.410 --> 01:06:00.130
There's never a moment where Andy gets what he needed.
安迪从未得到他真正需要的东西。

1332
01:06:00.130 --> 01:06:04.090
I was so uncomfortable this whole time.
我全程都感到非常不适。

1333
01:06:04.410 --> 01:06:14.010
Well, he doesn't get what he needs from his parents, but kind of like Michael Scott, his co-workers are becoming his family.
嗯，他确实没能从父母那里得到他需要的，但就像迈克尔·斯科特一样，他的同事们正在成为他的家人。

1334
01:06:14.270 --> 01:06:15.510
Did you see that parallel?
你看出这种相似之处了吗？

1335
01:06:15.830 --> 01:06:17.170
A little bit.
有一点。

1336
01:06:17.410 --> 01:06:18.510
A little bit.
有一点。

1337
01:06:18.850 --> 01:06:26.910
But I'm not imagining that Andy is going home after this garden party not being like kind of still wounded.
但我并不认为安迪在参加完这次花园派对回家后，就不会感到受伤了。

1338
01:06:27.330 --> 01:06:28.190
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

1339
01:06:28.610 --> 01:06:29.510
I don't know.
我不知道。

1340
01:06:30.130 --> 01:06:36.670
Well, to break up this tragedy with a little comedy, Moe's is going to, what?
好吧，为了用一点喜剧来缓解这种悲剧色彩，莫斯打算，怎么着？

1341
01:06:36.890 --> 01:06:40.670
He's going to jump over the row of cars in a Vespa?
他要骑着韦士柏摩托车飞跃那一排汽车吗？

1342
01:06:40.890 --> 01:06:41.150
What?
什么？

1343
01:06:41.550 --> 01:06:43.930
He's going to have his Evel Knievel moment.
他要上演属于他的埃维尔·克尼维尔时刻。

1344
01:06:44.390 --> 01:06:44.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1345
01:06:45.210 --> 01:06:46.050
It doesn't make it.
他没成功。

1346
01:06:46.190 --> 01:06:48.690
So then he just runs across the top of it.
所以他最后直接从车顶上跑了过去。

1347
01:06:49.350 --> 01:06:51.730
A fan question from Amanda in Ontario.
来自安大略省阿曼达的粉丝提问。

1348
01:06:51.750 --> 01:06:56.750
What was the process behind the stunt where Moe's runs across the roofs of the car?
莫斯在车顶上奔跑的那个特技，背后的制作过程是怎样的？

1349
01:06:56.750 --> 01:07:07.070
Well, Steve Burgess said there was a lot of prep involved and that we originally really did want to have Moe's ride the scooter across the cars.
嗯，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说这涉及大量的准备工作，而且我们最初确实想让莫斯骑着滑板车穿过那些车。

1350
01:07:07.070 --> 01:07:09.390
But Universal said no.
但环球影业拒绝了。

1351
01:07:09.650 --> 01:07:12.430
They said it would cause too much damage to the cars.
他们说那样会对车子造成太大的损坏。

1352
01:07:12.430 --> 01:07:13.830
It would be too expensive.
那样太贵了。

1353
01:07:14.210 --> 01:07:16.690
They weren't concerned, I guess, about the safety.
我想他们并不关心安全问题。

1354
01:07:16.870 --> 01:07:18.730
They were concerned about the cost of that.
他们关心的是那方面的成本。

1355
01:07:18.730 --> 01:07:20.910
Yeah, that's what it sounds like.
没错，听起来确实是这样。

1356
01:07:21.070 --> 01:07:28.130
So as an alternative, they decided to have not Mike Schur, but a stunt double run across the cars.
所以作为替代方案，他们决定不让迈克·舒尔，而是找个替身演员跑过车顶。

1357
01:07:28.370 --> 01:07:36.030
But Steve Burgess said that actually caused quite a bit of damage and was very costly anyway.
但史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，那实际上也造成了相当大的损坏，而且无论如何都很昂贵。

1358
01:07:36.610 --> 01:07:39.430
Just a person running on the top of the cars.
就只是一个人在车顶上跑。

1359
01:07:39.430 --> 01:07:42.290
It dented in the tops of the cars.
那把车顶都踩凹了。

1360
01:07:42.690 --> 01:07:48.230
I want to say that I thought the stunt guy playing Moe's did an excellent job of running like Moe's.
我想说，我觉得那个扮演莫斯的特技演员在模仿莫斯跑步方面做得非常出色。

1361
01:07:48.590 --> 01:07:49.990
It was a very good Moe's run.
那是一次非常棒的莫斯式奔跑。

1362
01:07:50.090 --> 01:07:52.810
Yeah, because Mike Schur has a weird run as Moe's.
没错，因为迈克·舒尔扮演莫斯时跑步姿势很奇怪。

1363
01:07:52.810 --> 01:07:53.190
I know.
我知道。

1364
01:07:53.350 --> 01:07:54.590
This guy really sold it.
这家伙演得真到位。

1365
01:07:55.210 --> 01:08:00.770
Robert, California, and Dwight have a very funny exchange where, you know, Dwight's talking about the beet farm.
罗伯特·加州和德怀特有一段非常有趣的对话，你知道的，德怀特在谈论甜菜农场。

1366
01:08:01.050 --> 01:08:02.850
And Robert's like, forget the beets.
然后罗伯特说，别提什么甜菜了。

1367
01:08:03.210 --> 01:08:04.850
You should rent this place out.
你应该把这个地方租出去。

1368
01:08:04.850 --> 01:08:08.970
I would pay a considerable amount of money to have my birthday party here.
我会花一大笔钱在这里举办我的生日派对。

1369
01:08:09.490 --> 01:08:14.870
And then Dwight goes into great detail about all the different birthday packages they offer.
然后德怀特非常详细地介绍了他们提供的各种生日套餐。

1370
01:08:14.870 --> 01:08:17.850
And they all include a lot of goats.
而且它们都包含大量的山羊。

1371
01:08:18.170 --> 01:08:18.870
A lot of goats.
大量的山羊。

1372
01:08:18.950 --> 01:08:19.910
Some more than others.
有的比其他的多。

1373
01:08:20.150 --> 01:08:21.250
Some are all goats.
有的全是山羊。

1374
01:08:21.650 --> 01:08:23.070
Some are just a few goats.
有的只有几只山羊。

1375
01:08:23.330 --> 01:08:25.450
Robert, California has a line that's so funny.
罗伯特·加州有一句台词太搞笑了。

1376
01:08:25.590 --> 01:08:29.170
He's like, why are you talking to me about these goats?
他说，你为什么要跟我谈论这些山羊？

1377
01:08:29.330 --> 01:08:33.350
Yeah, he said you spend way too much time explaining the goats.
没错，他说你花太多时间解释这些山羊了。

1378
01:08:33.350 --> 01:08:35.170
Yeah, I just loved it.
是啊，我太喜欢这段了。

1379
01:08:35.170 --> 01:08:35.770
I loved it too.
我也很喜欢。

1380
01:08:36.050 --> 01:08:38.830
He's going to offer to get Robert some exotic meats.
他打算提议给罗伯特弄些异国肉类。

1381
01:08:39.030 --> 01:08:41.950
And then when Robert walks away, he says they're all goat.
然后当罗伯特走开时，他说那些肉其实全是山羊肉。

1382
01:08:42.370 --> 01:08:42.810
Yeah.
没错。

1383
01:08:43.050 --> 01:08:50.990
I don't know if this was from the mind of Justin Spitzer or if this was a bit that was written by a breakout room with one of the writers, but it was fantastic.
我不知道这是贾斯汀·斯皮策的想法，还是编剧组里某位编剧写出的桥段，但它太精彩了。

1384
01:08:51.370 --> 01:08:52.470
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1385
01:08:52.570 --> 01:08:59.850
I went to deleted scenes hoping that it was extended, that there was more Robert, California, and Dwight discussing goats, but there wasn't.
我去看过删减片段，希望能看到加长版，希望能有更多罗伯特·加州和德怀特讨论山羊的内容，但并没有。

1386
01:09:00.550 --> 01:09:04.810
Well, if you wanted to get your heart broken, the next scene is going to do it.
好吧，如果你想体验心碎的感觉，接下来的场景绝对会让你如愿。

1387
01:09:05.670 --> 01:09:06.390
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

1388
01:09:06.830 --> 01:09:07.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1389
01:09:08.510 --> 01:09:17.130
Andy is talking to Cece, and his dad comes in and just really just belittles him just horribly.
安迪正在和西西说话，他爸爸进来了，对他进行了极其恶劣的贬低。

1390
01:09:17.130 --> 01:09:24.650
And the whole time it's over the baby monitor, we find out that Oscar and Daryl and Pam and Jim and Aaron have overheard the whole conversation.
而这一切都通过婴儿监视器传了出去，我们发现奥斯卡、达里尔、帕姆、吉姆和亚伦听到了整个谈话过程。

1391
01:09:25.050 --> 01:09:30.690
He's told him he's not proud of him, that he's the manager of a rinky dink paper company in Scranton.
他告诉安迪他不为他感到骄傲，说他只是斯克兰顿一家破烂造纸公司的经理。

1392
01:09:31.190 --> 01:09:32.170
Just as horrible.
简直太可怕了。

1393
01:09:32.170 --> 01:09:34.610
And then his parents leave.
然后他的父母就离开了。

1394
01:09:35.270 --> 01:09:36.070
That's it.
就这样。

1395
01:09:36.110 --> 01:09:38.010
There is no hug.
没有拥抱。

1396
01:09:38.190 --> 01:09:39.670
There's no, we're proud of you anyway.
没有那种“无论如何我们都为你骄傲”的话。

1397
01:09:39.990 --> 01:09:41.330
There's nothing positive.
没有任何积极的东西。

1398
01:09:41.690 --> 01:09:47.550
I did love the parents' talking head because I absolutely loved it when Dee Wallace said the sandwiches were dry.
我确实很喜欢他父母的采访片段，因为当迪·华莱士说三明治太干的时候，我简直太喜欢了。

1399
01:09:47.910 --> 01:09:50.470
I really loved it.
我真的很喜欢。

1400
01:09:50.470 --> 01:09:52.410
It was a very, like, parents' moment.
那非常有那种……父母的感觉。

1401
01:09:52.570 --> 01:10:01.090
Like, especially if you've planned your wedding, there's always some aunt and uncle or someone that has a comment that's like, well, I liked everything, but, you know,
比如，特别是如果你筹划过婚礼，总会有那么一两个叔叔阿姨或者什么人会发表意见，说什么，嗯，我什么都挺喜欢的，但是，你知道，

1402
01:10:01.470 --> 01:10:02.490
the bread was hard.
面包太硬了。

1403
01:10:03.550 --> 01:10:04.270
It's true.
确实如此。

1404
01:10:04.910 --> 01:10:09.330
Then we have what I think is a little bit of a redemption moment for Andy.
接下来是安迪的一个救赎时刻，我是这么认为的。

1405
01:10:09.930 --> 01:10:11.070
Everyone is hanging out.
大家都在一起闲逛。

1406
01:10:11.210 --> 01:10:12.370
It's very casual now.
现在气氛非常随意。

1407
01:10:12.650 --> 01:10:13.850
Daryl is working the grill.
达里尔在烤架旁忙活。

1408
01:10:14.510 --> 01:10:23.090
Oscar tosses the nard dog, a cold one, and Andy sits down on a picnic blanket, and it feels warm and cozy and so friendly.
奥斯卡扔给“纳德狗”一瓶冰镇啤酒，安迪坐在野餐垫上，感觉既温暖舒适又非常友好。

1409
01:10:23.550 --> 01:10:26.150
And boy, did Andy need this at the end of this day.
天哪，安迪在这一天结束时太需要这个了。

1410
01:10:26.250 --> 01:10:26.730
It's true.
确实如此。

1411
01:10:26.970 --> 01:10:30.850
We're going to have a final moment from Dwight as well, a final performance.
我们还要看德怀特最后的时刻，一场最后的表演。

1412
01:10:31.230 --> 01:10:35.530
It is a torch dance, a fire dance with the staff.
那是一场火炬舞，一场拿着棍棒的火舞。

1413
01:10:36.070 --> 01:10:40.890
This was, of course, from James Trickington's book about closing ceremonies.
这当然是出自詹姆斯·特里金顿关于闭幕式的书里。

1414
01:10:40.890 --> 01:10:42.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1415
01:10:42.210 --> 01:10:44.270
We had a fan question from Rebecca G.
我们收到一个来自德克萨斯州丽贝卡·G的粉丝提问，

1416
01:10:44.270 --> 01:10:49.470
in Texas who said, how long did it take for Rainn Wilson to learn the dance at the end of the episode?
她问，雷恩·威尔森学这一集结尾的舞蹈花了多久？

1417
01:10:49.770 --> 01:10:50.630
And Ryan S.
还有来自马萨诸塞州的瑞安·S，

1418
01:10:50.770 --> 01:10:57.250
from Massachusetts would like to know how many safety meetings were there about the use of fire in the closing ceremonies.
想知道关于闭幕式使用火的环节开了多少次安全会议。

1419
01:10:57.570 --> 01:11:02.870
Steve Burgess said that those dancers were an actual fire dance group.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说那些舞者是专业的火舞团。

1420
01:11:03.510 --> 01:11:04.070
Amazing.
太棒了。

1421
01:11:04.070 --> 01:11:06.730
And that Marianne Kellogg was our choreographer.
而且玛丽安·凯洛格是我们的编舞。

1422
01:11:07.370 --> 01:11:16.550
He said Rainn Wilson learned that choreography and worked with the fire dancers for a couple of hours earlier that morning in order to do that scene.
他说雷恩·威尔森那天早上提前几个小时学会了编舞，并与火舞者们进行了排练，才完成了那个场景。

1423
01:11:16.750 --> 01:11:21.630
And as far as safety, Steve Burgess said we had a lot of safety meetings all the time.
至于安全方面，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说我们一直都在开很多安全会议。

1424
01:11:21.770 --> 01:11:25.790
We had a big one first thing in the morning where we talked all about the day.
我们一大早就在开一个大型会议，讨论全天的安排。

1425
01:11:25.790 --> 01:11:34.510
I believe he reiterated the rattlesnakes, he reiterated the bees, he told us to hydrate, and he mentioned that later in the day we would have fire.
我相信他重申了响尾蛇的事，重申了蜜蜂的事，告诉我们要补充水分，还提到当天晚些时候会有火。

1426
01:11:34.770 --> 01:11:40.990
I remember our morning safety meeting and I remember them introducing us to our snake wrangler.
我记得我们的早间安全会议，也记得他们把驯蛇师介绍给我们认识。

1427
01:11:41.110 --> 01:11:41.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1428
01:11:41.430 --> 01:11:48.850
Yes, I remember it because I'll never forget, you know, if you get bit by a rattlesnake,
是的，我记得，因为我永远不会忘记，你知道，如果你被响尾蛇咬了，

1429
01:11:49.010 --> 01:11:56.850
you are not supposed to run because that makes the venom move more quickly through your system.
你不应该奔跑，因为那会让毒液在你的身体里扩散得更快。

1430
01:11:57.030 --> 01:12:03.170
You're not supposed to have a person who has been bit by a rattlesnake move themselves out of the area.
你不应该让被响尾蛇咬伤的人自己离开现场。

1431
01:12:03.170 --> 01:12:07.870
Yeah, you are supposed to get someone to carry them out.
没错，你应该找人把他们抬出去。

1432
01:12:08.150 --> 01:12:14.670
And that was the whole thing, that it was like you're supposed to scream for help so that you can be carried out of the area.
重点就在这儿，你应该大声呼救，这样才能被抬离现场。

1433
01:12:14.910 --> 01:12:18.690
I just remember the guy had these really tall boots on.
我只记得那个人穿着那种特别高的靴子。

1434
01:12:19.030 --> 01:12:24.970
And you and I were walking around in little high heels or flats and I was like, should we all have the tall boots?
而你和我穿着小高跟鞋或平底鞋走来走去，我就想，我们是不是都该穿那种高靴子？

1435
01:12:24.990 --> 01:12:25.350
Yes.
是的。

1436
01:12:25.550 --> 01:12:26.390
Where are the boots?
靴子在哪儿呢？

1437
01:12:26.410 --> 01:12:27.350
I want some boots.
我也想要双靴子。

1438
01:12:28.310 --> 01:12:32.870
Steve said we also fireproofed all of the wardrobe for the fire dancers.
史蒂夫说我们还对火舞者的所有服装进行了防火处理。

1439
01:12:33.450 --> 01:12:37.310
And we had another safety meeting right before the fire dance started.
而且在火舞开始前，我们又开了一次安全会议。

1440
01:12:37.670 --> 01:12:39.230
And that's how it all went down.
事情就是这样发生的。

1441
01:12:39.550 --> 01:12:47.950
Before our rewatch is done of the office, I really want Kelly Cantley to come on and I want her to do a full safety meeting on the podcaSt.
在我们的《办公室》重温结束之前，我真的想请凯莉·坎特利来，我想让她在播客上做一次完整的安全会议。

1442
01:12:48.310 --> 01:12:48.510
Absolutely.
绝对没问题。

1443
01:12:48.950 --> 01:12:50.150
It has to happen.
一定要实现。

1444
01:12:50.690 --> 01:12:52.510
This episode ends with a tag.
这一集以一个彩蛋结束。

1445
01:12:52.690 --> 01:12:54.510
It is Jim pranking Dwight.
是吉姆捉弄德怀特。

1446
01:12:54.770 --> 01:12:57.110
This prank made more sense to me, okay?
这个恶作剧我能看懂，好吗？

1447
01:12:57.390 --> 01:13:01.950
He's just going to enter the party over and over so that Dwight is constantly having to say,
他就是不断地进入派对现场，搞得德怀特不得不一直说，

1448
01:13:01.950 --> 01:13:03.010
Jim Halpert.
吉姆·哈珀特。

1449
01:13:03.770 --> 01:13:07.770
And he's like asking him questions like, who's the best salesman in the branch?
然后他问他一些问题，比如，分部最好的销售员是谁？

1450
01:13:07.910 --> 01:13:10.450
And then he exits and he comes back in, Jim Halpert.
接着他走出去，又走进来，吉姆·哈珀特。

1451
01:13:10.830 --> 01:13:12.710
And he just does this over and over.
他就是这样一遍又一遍地做。

1452
01:13:13.090 --> 01:13:17.270
I loved this whole bit of Rain announcing everyone and shouting as Dwight.
我很喜欢雷恩宣布每个人的名字并模仿德怀特大喊大叫的那一段。

1453
01:13:17.530 --> 01:13:19.270
I thought it was a fun way to end the episode.
我觉得这是结束这一集的一种有趣方式。

1454
01:13:19.270 --> 01:13:27.410
I want to say that I thought that this garden party with all of these weird elements was actually quite charming and interesting.
我想说，我觉得这场包含各种奇怪元素的花园派对其实相当迷人且有趣。

1455
01:13:27.870 --> 01:13:32.050
And like Robert California, I would be interested in having that party.
而且就像罗伯特·加利福尼亚一样，我也很有兴趣举办那样的派对。

1456
01:13:32.450 --> 01:13:33.630
Forget the beats.
忘了那些节拍吧。

1457
01:13:33.850 --> 01:13:36.430
Focus on parties minus the goats.
专注于派对，去掉山羊。

1458
01:13:37.390 --> 01:13:37.790
Exactly.
没错。

1459
01:13:38.390 --> 01:13:38.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1460
01:13:38.790 --> 01:13:40.310
Well, there you have it, everybody.
好了，各位，以上就是全部内容了。

1461
01:13:40.490 --> 01:13:41.250
That was garden party.
这就是《花园派对》那一集。

1462
01:13:41.970 --> 01:13:43.310
Thanks so much for listening.
非常感谢大家的收听。

1463
01:13:43.530 --> 01:13:46.570
Thank you so much to Josh Groban for stopping by.
非常感谢乔什·格罗班能来做客。

1464
01:13:46.810 --> 01:13:48.130
What an absolute delight.
真是太令人愉快了。

1465
01:13:48.550 --> 01:13:52.130
And thank you to Steve Burgess for all his great insider info.
也感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯提供的所有精彩内幕信息。

1466
01:13:52.850 --> 01:13:53.330
Yes.
是的。

1467
01:13:53.550 --> 01:13:56.130
And next week we will be back with Spooked.
下周我们将回归，讨论《惊吓》那一集。

1468
01:13:56.350 --> 01:13:57.750
Oh, that's a Halloween episode.
哦，那是万圣节特辑。

1469
01:13:58.570 --> 01:13:58.930
Yum.
棒极了。

1470
01:13:59.310 --> 01:14:00.270
Halloween in June.
六月的万圣节。

1471
01:14:00.930 --> 01:14:01.910
Bye, you guys.
再见，大家。

1472
01:14:02.110 --> 01:14:02.530
Bye.
再见。

